{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1166761-balancing-wards-signs-dispels-supernal-veil","id":1166761,"title":"Balancing Wards+Signs & Dispels & Supernal Veil","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-11T12:03:58-08:00","id":1166761,"title":"Balancing Wards+Signs & Dispels & Supernal Veil","content":"So I'm running a sprawling multi-year crossover campaign that started as Hunter, then became effectively Werewolf and now I'm trying to mix in some Mage. Mage is, of course, difficult to balance with other lines. But I'm starting to be amazed at how difficult it is to balance with itself. I could really do with some help. Please don't interpret my opinionated bluntness for douchery.<br /> <br /> So how do you guys make mage combat actually work? I'll highlight some special things:<br /> <br /> Exceptional successes break Withstand - I don't even know where to start with this. At the point where a mage can cast an Adept direct damage spell, they can cast it combined with itself as a praxis and reliably get an exceptional... dealing minimum 8 lethal (aggravated if they spring for 2 mana) bypassing W/S. And, as we all know, direct damage spells are supposed to be the laziest and least effective spells.<br /> <br /> My tentative houserule is that nothing that would spell certain death (including taking them out of the fight) for anyone can bypass resistance, be it W/S or something else. Anybody else have any suggestions?<br /> <br /> Random question: Can you use a Mudra without casting a rote? In other words, can you take the skill bonus as a +X yantra while casting as a praxis?<br /> <br /> Wards &amp; Signs subject vs area - The description says that it only works on spells that directly target the subject. The breadth of interpretation here means that W/S is either extremely powerful or extremely powerless. For instance, why not turn your boring direct damage subject spell into a boring direct damage area spell hitting &quot;arm's reach from a central point&quot;? Or take the -2 to make it &quot;the size of a small room&quot;? Does this only affect spells that specify a subject, then? That's not a very imposing list.<br /> <br /> Speaking of area spells how the hell do you work that - Does defense or dodge apply to a fireball that literally engulfs an entire room? If not, why not do this all the time?<br /> <br /> What does W/S actually cover - It shields you from hostile magic: only awakened magic, I guess? Does it shield your spells from dispels? The things you are currently wearing or carrying? The air you are about to breathe into your lungs? Does it shield you from attainments?<br /> <br /> Dispels how do they do - SO, barring archmagi, the maximum Withstand for a dispel is exactly 7 with 5 Arcana and +2 from Advanced Potency. That is... unless Wards &amp; Signs applies to spells. If so, does W/S apply to all the spells on a given mage or just each spell that is its subject? Can Wards &amp; Signs apply to all spells and individuals and objects in a static area like a Sanctum? In any of those cases, can Wards &amp; Signs apply to dispels against itself? Also, can you area instead of subject dispel?<br /> <br /> Also: Does Supernal Dispellation only apply to Awakened magic? Asking for a werewolf friend. My gut says no, but that a Spirit 4 creative thaumaturgy could dispel various wolf-related stuff and same for Death with vampers. Either that or it's a combined Prime + relevant arcana etc etc.<br /> <br /> OH HO HO Supernal Veil is stronk or maybe not - So in order to dispel a spell you have to perceive it, right? Well what if the other mage has indefinite Supernal Veil on and you fail on your COW? Does that mean that it's impossible to dispel lack of perception from supernal veil because you can't perceive it? Does it apply to every spell on a given subject? Does it apply to itself? Can it apply to everything inside a static area? This is either very powerful or not powerful at all.<br /> <br /> Is there a possible Clash of Wills shield spell for prime? - Time, Mind, Space, Death, Spirit and Fate all have spells that force a COW against magic of their Arcanum. Can similar ones be made for the other ones? Speaking of: what does Soul Armor apply against that Ghost Shield wouldn't???<br /> <br /> Never having run it before, it's difficult to conceptualize how magical combat actually works. I'm inclined towards &quot;It doesn't and it's just creative MTP megadeath rocket tag which is why arcane duels exist.&quot; I mean... how was this stuff dealt with in playtesting? In my head it all looks like &quot;Whoever wins initiative casts combined dispel vs Wards+Signs and some form of instant death/disabling with advanced scaling for TPK.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Final notes: my probationary houserules are &quot;spells that cause instagib or scene-long stunlock are always withstood&quot;, &quot;advanced potency spells always withstand&quot;, &quot;supernatural power stats count as an extra withstand rating&quot; and &quot;ephemerals withstand with resistance because allowing entry-level mages to browbeat rank 5 'minor gods' with 6 potency is f***ing insane.&quot; What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11153-bonerstorm","name":"bonerstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-11T13:02:55-08:00","id":1166776,"title":"","content":"While I do have a bunch of house rules to fix some of the issues you bring up, in my campaigns I rarely if ever use &quot;combat as a sport&quot; mechanics. Most mages in my universe can and will instantly and absurdly kill you if you mess with them enough and they took time to prepare the appropriate spell. This causes there to be a lot of politics created in an attempt to prevent a drastic depopulation of Awakened. Also, Awakened tend to have complicated long-term goals, which makes most of them want to avoid getting into deadly arcane combat. Also if you kill the wrong mage, you could end up labeled as a Banisher and that's going to make your plans a bit harder to complete for sure. And yes, you can blow up a whole building kinda easily, but it's not like you get to use that sort of power too often (sometimes your cabalmates will get nervous when they realize you can mind control a whole bar to messily kill and cleanup anyone you want inside it and make sure no one will remember it). <br /> <br /> Random answers: You can't get the yantra bonus of a mudra is you don't have the rote. I don't think you can combine a spell with itself, as it would normally not be allowed to stack with itself. In my house rules, direct damage spells use successes as damage instead of potency (I only use potency to check for Withstand and nothing more since I've rewritten every spell in the book not to use potency), thus making damage a bit more unpredictable. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-11T13:05:45-08:00","id":1166778,"title":"","content":"That's a lot of questions. There's a bit of stream of consciousness going on in your post...<ul><li>The first thing is that it's very difficult to balance the game lines across one another. They were not designed to be balanced with each other.</li> <li>You cannot use Mudras without casting a Rote.</li> <li>I personally take the Wards and Signs text to mean someone falling directly under a spell's effect, rather than the after-effect of a spell, such as a telekinetically thrown trash can hitting you.</li> <li>You cannot dodge spells with Area targeting. Anyone who enters the area is automatically affected by the spell. Aimed spells, on the other hand, allow one to apply Defense. Why not do Area spells all the time? It requires Reach (usually 2) to be useful. It cannot discriminate targets (unless you add Fate 2). These are very good reasons to not use Area spells all the time.</li> <li>Wards and Signs shields from Awakened Magic and possibly other effects the ST rules that fall under the purview of Prime. It does not protect against Attainments, as Attainments are explicitly not magical. It will only shield your spells from dispellation if you cast Wards and Signs on those spells.</li> <li>There is nothing stopping you from casting Wards and Signs on an ongoing spell to protect it. However, the rules for multiple Withstands comes into play. When stacking Withstands, only the highest applies, and you get +1 from each other source of Withstand. Personally I would also rule that spell stacking rules do not allow multiple Wards and Signs to further increase the Withstand--only the highest Wards and Signs would apply.</li> <li>Supernal Dispellation is the same as Dispel Magic but without the Arcanum requirement. Awakened Magic is explicitly under the purview of Prime. Werewolf Gifts are not (however, they are under the purview of Spirit, as you say). Once you start doing crossovers, it is a bit up to ST fiat. I would not allow Dispellation to affect the powers of other templates, unless the appropriate conjunctional Arcanum was added at 4 dots (Practice of Patterning).</li> <li>When mages hit a Clash of Wills, they know that the spell is clashing. However, they do not know what it is clashing with. But then again, with a bit of logic, you could probably figure out what it's clashing against, as long as you have enough contextual information (e.g. you know you're up against a mage). If you did an AOE dispellation and the mage with Supernal Veil is within the area, Supernal Veil would be affected, as Area spells are not reliant on perception to affect targets--perhaps barring some kind of Creative Thaumaturgy Fate or Space(?) Veiling effect.</li> <li>There is no Clash of Wills Shielding spell in Prime, possibly for balance reasons.</li> <li>Ghost Shield can protect against Death magic that affects the soul, but Soul Armor can protect against <i>any </i>magic that can affect the soul. It's a bit situational but still useful.</li> <li>The Duel Arcane was invented because mages are powerhouses. Once mages get 4 dots in an Arcanum, then real combat starts to become a lot more lethal. But keep in mind you don't always know what Potency you need on dispellation. Dangerous combat is also why mages like to avoid direct confrontation, and be prepared.</li> <li>Adding Supernatural Tolerance trait to Withstand will nerf mages far too much. The rulebook explicitly says not to do this.</li> <li>Getting potency 6 as a starting mage is not very easy if you want to actually be able to cast your spell, even with a 15 hour ritual.</li> </ul><br /> Mages will always eclipse other templates in terms of power. Even starting mages can travel back in time by multiple Scenes, or traipse around the universe. Demons can sort of compete with them, apparently. But werewolves and vampires are a tier below when it comes to pure mechanical power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-11T13:09:38-08:00","id":1166781,"title":"","content":"You can\u2019t combine cast a damage spell with itself and double the damage you\u2019re putting out. Second, direct damage spells don\u2019t deal with Withstand unless a Reach has been spent to apply a Tilt.<br /> <br /> You can\u2019t apply a Mudra bonus to a spell that isn\u2019t a Rote.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 12-12-2017, 04:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-11T13:20:51-08:00","id":1166787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1166761-balancing-wards-signs-dispels-supernal-veil?p=1166781#post1166781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can\u2019t combine cast a damage spell with itself and double the damage you\u2019re putting out. Second, direct damage spells don\u2019t deal with Withstand unless a Reach has been spent to apply a Tilt.<br /> <br /> You can\u2019t apply a Mustafa bonus to a spell that isn\u2019t a Rote.</div> </div> </div> </div>Easiest one to reply to:<br /> 1) Where's the rule that says you can't combine a damage spell with itself? OK, let's say you can't. Why can't (as an Obrimos) I combine Celestial Fire with Thunderbolt to accomplish the exact same thing?<br /> <br /> 2) Yeah I was talking about Withstand from Wards &amp; Signs. Basically, RAW, you can have an indefinite potency 20 Wards &amp; Signs up but it will do nothing against a spell with an exceptional success UNLESS it's an Arcana 5 instagib spell (which is called out as always resisted).<br /> <br /> 3) Mudras are yantras. I don't see anything in the rules that say you can't use the Mudra yantra without casting as a rote? You definitely can't cast as a rote (gaining 5 arcana worth of reach and, if you created it, rote on the spellcasting roll) while casting as a praxis... but there's nothing in the rules about only being able to use the Mudra while casting as a rote.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11153-bonerstorm","name":"bonerstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-11T13:25:52-08:00","id":1166789,"title":"","content":"The question about combined damage spells came up and was answered on the forums, essentially it boils down to the fact that if you cast two spells with identical Potency and purpose only one will take effect. On spells with Duration this will cause one spell to essentially be a backup that will kick in if the \u201cactive\u201d one is dispelled. On an instant spell like a damage spell though only one instance will take effect.<br /> <br /> Mudras are specifically called out as being part of the rote creation process which is why they only work with Rotes.<br /> <br /> Bypassing Withstand is one effect on the menu of effects you can achieve with an Exceptional Success, it doesn\u2019t have to be selected or allowed if the ST doesn\u2019t think it thematically appropriate to the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 12-11-2017, 04:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-11T13:52:09-08:00","id":1166800,"title":"","content":"1<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>projectmoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1166761-balancing-wards-signs-dispels-supernal-veil?p=1166778#post1166778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a lot of questions. There's a bit of stream of consciousness going on in your post...<ul><li>The first thing is that it's very difficult to balance the game lines across one another. They were not designed to be balanced with each other.</li> <li>You cannot use Mudras without casting a Rote.</li> <li>I personally take the Wards and Signs text to mean someone falling directly under a spell's effect, rather than the after-effect of a spell, such as a telekinetically thrown trash can hitting you.</li> <li>You cannot dodge spells with Area targeting. Anyone who enters the area is automatically affected by the spell. Aimed spells, on the other hand, allow one to apply Defense. Why not do Area spells all the time? It requires Reach (usually 2) to be useful. It cannot discriminate targets (unless you add Fate 2). These are very good reasons to not use Area spells all the time.</li> <li>Wards and Signs shields from Awakened Magic and possibly other effects the ST rules that fall under the purview of Prime. It does not protect against Attainments, as Attainments are explicitly not magical. It will only shield your spells from dispellation if you cast Wards and Signs on those spells.</li> <li>There is nothing stopping you from casting Wards and Signs on an ongoing spell to protect it. However, the rules for multiple Withstands comes into play. When stacking Withstands, only the highest applies, and you get +1 from each other source of Withstand. Personally I would also rule that spell stacking rules do not allow multiple Wards and Signs to further increase the Withstand--only the highest Wards and Signs would apply.</li> <li>Supernal Dispellation is the same as Dispel Magic but without the Arcanum requirement. Awakened Magic is explicitly under the purview of Prime. Werewolf Gifts are not (however, they are under the purview of Spirit, as you say). Once you start doing crossovers, it is a bit up to ST fiat. I would not allow Dispellation to affect the powers of other templates, unless the appropriate conjunctional Arcanum was added at 4 dots (Practice of Patterning).</li> <li>When mages hit a Clash of Wills, they know that the spell is clashing. However, they do not know what it is clashing with. But then again, with a bit of logic, you could probably figure out what it's clashing against, as long as you have enough contextual information (e.g. you know you're up against a mage). If you did an AOE dispellation and the mage with Supernal Veil is within the area, Supernal Veil would be affected, as Area spells are not reliant on perception to affect targets--perhaps barring some kind of Creative Thaumaturgy Fate or Space(?) Veiling effect.</li> <li>There is no Clash of Wills Shielding spell in Prime, possibly for balance reasons.</li> <li>Ghost Shield can protect against Death magic that affects the soul, but Soul Armor can protect against <i>any </i>magic that can affect the soul. It's a bit situational but still useful.</li> <li>The Duel Arcane was invented because mages are powerhouses. Once mages get 4 dots in an Arcanum, then real combat starts to become a lot more lethal. But keep in mind you don't always know what Potency you need on dispellation. Dangerous combat is also why mages like to avoid direct confrontation, and be prepared.</li> <li>Adding Supernatural Tolerance trait to Withstand will nerf mages far too much. The rulebook explicitly says not to do this.</li> <li>Getting potency 6 as a starting mage is not very easy if you want to actually be able to cast your spell, even with a 15 hour ritual.</li> </ul>Mages will always eclipse other templates in terms of power. Even starting mages can travel back in time by multiple Scenes, or traipse around the universe. Demons can sort of compete with them, apparently. But werewolves and vampires are a tier below when it comes to pure mechanical power.</div> </div> </div> </div>You cannot use Mudras without casting a Rote. -<br /> <br /> Where does it say this in the rules? Mudras are listed as yantras and nothing in the yantra section says they are only usable when casting as a rote.<br /> <br /> <br /> I personally take the Wards and Signs text to mean someone falling directly under a spell's effect, rather than the after-effect of a spell, such as a telekinetically thrown trash can hitting you.<br /> <br /> I dig that. But my questions are things like<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />oes W/S protect just the mage or also the mage's possessions and spells? This is important because &quot;hostile magic&quot; could mean &quot;everything in on and of my person is sacrosanct&quot; or it could mean &quot;literally you can't cast a spell where I am explicitly named the subject, rather than my spells or my wand or my pants or the air around my face.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> You cannot dodge spells with Area targeting. Anyone who enters the area is automatically affected by the spell. Aimed spells, on the other hand, allow one to apply Defense. Why not do Area spells all the time? It requires Reach (usually 2) to be useful. It cannot discriminate targets (unless you add Fate 2). These are very good reasons to not use Area spells all the time.<br /> <br /> Ummm... could you explain what you mean about Reach 2? It's literally a -2 casting roll penalty to cast as an area encompassing &quot;a small room&quot; with standard scale and it costs absolutely nothing to go from a targeted spell to an area spell. Also... entering areas? What about casting a room-sized fireball at a room-sized area where your enemy already is? That's generally how these things go.<br /> <br /> <br /> Wards and Signs shields from Awakened Magic and possibly other effects the ST rules that fall under the purview of Prime. It does not protect against Attainments, as Attainments are explicitly not magical. It will only shield your spells from dispellation if you cast Wards and Signs on those spells.<br /> <br /> Where does it say that Attainments are non-magical? All it says is that the can't be supernally dispelled or countered and isn't subject to the Lie... explicitly legacy attainments &quot;do not count as *obvious* magic&quot;... not that they can't be withstood. Also not that they can't be subject to, for instance, a clash of wills from a Supernal spell power.<br /> <br /> <br /> When mages hit a Clash of Wills, they know that the spell is clashing. However, they do not know what it is clashing with. But then again, with a bit of logic, you could probably figure out what it's clashing against, as long as you have enough contextual information (e.g. you know you're up against a mage). If you did an AOE dispellation and the mage with Supernal Veil is within the area, Supernal Veil would be affected, as Area spells are not reliant on perception to affect targets--perhaps barring some kind of Creative Thaumaturgy Fate or Space(?) Veiling effect.<br /> <br /> Is it possible to do an AOE dispel? In that case, would that stack all of the Withstand +1's from every spell in that area? The rules say explicitly that different *subjects* of a spell withstand separately... but nothing about different things inside an area. Supernal Dispellation is a subject-specifying spell and I can see a &quot;small room-sized&quot; dispel affecting all spells inside equally being extremely OP.<br /> <br /> <br /> Adding Supernatural Tolerance trait to Withstand will nerf mages far too much. The rulebook explicitly says not to do this.<br /> <br /> Yes, it does say that. I'm really not convinced, though. A mage already has many ways of destroying an ancient BP 10 vampire without resorting to &quot;Oh... his stamina is just three? Poofed.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Getting potency 6 as a starting mage is not very easy if you want to actually be able to cast your spell, even with a 15 hour ritual.<br /> <br /> Are we reading the same 2E rulebook? Starting Potency is 3 from Arcana. Base dice pool is Gnosis 1 + Arcana 3 = 4. Add 3, 4 or 5 from rote Mudra with rote specialty. Right out the gate, you can take a -6 to increase to potency 6 while reducing your dice pool to 1, 2 or 3.... PLUS 3 from Willpower (which means you can reasonably expect it to cast). Then, if you have literally 3 more seconds... you can use High Speech for another +2 to your roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11153-bonerstorm","user":"bonerstorm","date":". 12-11-2017, 04:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11153-bonerstorm","name":"bonerstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-11T14:03:31-08:00","id":1166808,"title":"","content":"The rules about Mudras are in a subsection for the Yantra rules, it doesn\u2019t specifically disallow the use of Mudras on other kinds of spells, but it is implicit in the text because it only talks about using mudras in the context of Rotes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-11T15:33:51-08:00","id":1166841,"title":"","content":"&quot;When casting a Rote from memory, using an Order\u2019s recall techniques, the character may use dots in the associated Skill as a Yantra. The character must be free to make the mnemonic gestures to recall the Rote in order to benefit from the Skill bonus&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-11T17:35:06-08:00","id":1166861,"title":"","content":"Man..at least make some effort to present your questions in a readable manner. I'd love to try and help - I'm sure many people would - but you're asking a lot of questions in a nearly incoherent stream of consciousness that makes any attempt at actually sifting through your post for specific questions an exercise in frustration.<br /> <br /> To discuss a couple that I saw mentioned:<br /> <br /> 1) no, you can't dodge or apply Defense against any non-aimed spell, including area spells. Mages don't just always use AOEs because you can't choose the targets of an AOE, it affects all viable subjects in the area indiscriminately, which is often problematic.<br /> 2) No, you can't combine two of the same (or even different) direct damage spells to do double damage, this has been clarified by the devs. Search Dave's posts if you want to find the specific post.<br /> 3) Mudras are part of using a rote, they can't be used independently.<br /> 4) Wards &amp; Signs only applies to awakened magic (spells, attainments, etc). It adds Withstand, a mechanic no system besides Awakened magic even engages with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-11T18:06:08-08:00","id":1166865,"title":"","content":"Please format your post with the quote functionality. It's very difficult to decode otherwise.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bonerstorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1166761-balancing-wards-signs-dispels-supernal-veil?p=1166800#post1166800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1<br /> I dig that. But my questions are things like<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />oes W/S protect just the mage or also the mage's possessions and spells? This is important because &quot;hostile magic&quot; could mean &quot;everything in on and of my person is sacrosanct&quot; or it could mean &quot;literally you can't cast a spell where I am explicitly named the subject, rather than my spells or my wand or my pants or the air around my face.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>If you cast it on yourself, it protects you. If you cast it on your possessions, it protects those. If you cast it on your spells, it protects those. There is some wiggle room when it comes to this. Like at what point do you start splitting hairs on the subjects of a spell? Personally if it's something insignificant like clothes, I'd ignore it as a subject. But stuff like worn artifacts or imbued items, you may need to target separately as a subject. of the spell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ummm... could you explain what you mean about Reach 2? It's literally a -2 casting roll penalty to cast as an area encompassing &quot;a small room&quot; with standard scale and it costs absolutely nothing to go from a targeted spell to an area spell. Also... entering areas? What about casting a room-sized fireball at a room-sized area where your enemy already is? That's generally how these things go. </div> </div> </div>One Reach for sensory range, and another Reach for Advanced Scale. You at least need Sensory Range in most cases. You can take dice penalties, yes, but then that leaves you with less dice for other fun effects, like Potency. As for room-sized fireballs, yes, that will work at least a few times. But if the mages are clearing rooms like this all the time, the encounter needs to be run differently. Enemies are going to wise up eventually, and at least prepare tactically.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Where does it say that Attainments are non-magical? All it says is that the can't be supernally dispelled or countered and isn't subject to the Lie... explicitly legacy attainments &quot;do not count as *obvious* magic&quot;... not that they can't be withstood. Also not that they can't be subject to, for instance, a clash of wills from a Supernal spell power. </div> </div> </div>This is true. In fact, the Attainments chapter calls them out as magical effects. Legacy Attainments are a bit different, but I guess I read too far into the meaning of that. It says they're not any different than natural phenomena (although I guess still considered magical to an extent). Attainments can indeed be Withstood and subject to a Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is it possible to do an AOE dispel? In that case, would that stack all of the Withstand +1's from every spell in that area? The rules say explicitly that different *subjects* of a spell withstand separately... but nothing about different things inside an area. Supernal Dispellation is a subject-specifying spell and I can see a &quot;small room-sized&quot; dispel affecting all spells inside equally being extremely OP. </div> </div> </div>It is possible to an area casting of any spell. Anyone/anything inside an area spell is a subject: &quot;If using Area of Effect for Scale, the factor instead determines how large the area covered by the spell is, applying the spell effect to anyone or anything within.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, it does say that. I'm really not convinced, though. A mage already has many ways of destroying an ancient BP 10 vampire without resorting to &quot;Oh... his stamina is just three? Poofed.&quot; </div> </div> </div>A vampire at Blood Potency 10 isn't going to be out in the open for a mage to attack. Vampires, especially ones of that caliber, are master manipulators. The mage's social and family life will come to a bloody end long before he finds that vampire. And a Master (the only ones who can &quot;poof&quot; things with Making/Unmaking) is quite unstoppable, if prepared. This is by design.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are we reading the same 2E rulebook? Starting Potency is 3 from Arcana. Base dice pool is Gnosis 1 + Arcana 3 = 4. Add 3, 4 or 5 from rote Mudra with rote specialty. Right out the gate, you can take a -6 to increase to potency 6 while reducing your dice pool to 1, 2 or 3.... PLUS 3 from Willpower (which means you can reasonably expect it to cast). Then, if you have literally 3 more seconds... you can use High Speech for another +2 to your roll. </div> </div> </div>Yes, if you specialize hardcore in something, you will be able to get a lot out of it. But again this is missing story consequences. The character gives up other things in order to make this happen. And rank 5 spirits aren't going to take kindly to being controlled or enslaved. And even if a mage can control a level 5 spirit, that spirit's retaliation will be swift and dangerous if it did not agree to be controlled, not to say anything of its &quot;allies&quot; that lurk in the Shadow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-11T21:08:20-08:00","id":1166900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1166761-balancing-wards-signs-dispels-supernal-veil?p=1166841#post1166841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;When casting a Rote from memory, using an Order\u2019s recall techniques, the character may use dots in the associated Skill as a Yantra. The character must be free to make the mnemonic gestures to recall the Rote in order to benefit from the Skill bonus&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks guys! I also found this in the spellcasting appendix: (emphasis added)<br /> Rote: Gains free Reach as though character had five dots<br /> in Arcanum. ***May use Mudra Yantras.*** If cast out of Grimoire,<br /> cannot use instant casting and doubles ritual interval. If cast<br /> out of Grimoire or by creator, gains rote action quality (p. 214)<br /> on spellcasting roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11153-bonerstorm","name":"bonerstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-11T21:09:33-08:00","id":1166901,"title":"","content":"Sorry for my crappy formatting guys. I'll learn moar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11153-bonerstorm","name":"bonerstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T00:19:19-08:00","id":1166927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bonerstorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1166761-balancing-wards-signs-dispels-supernal-veil?p=1166901#post1166901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry for my crappy formatting guys. I'll learn moar.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Simple lesson to take from this, Dont cross the streams.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Final notes: my probationary houserules are &quot;spells that cause instagib or scene-long stunlock are always withstood&quot;, </div> </div> </div>Note that unmaking spells are always withstood when used on somebody so no need to house rule it. (though a ES can still ignore the withstand)<br /> <br /> An area dispel magic spell will dispel all spells within the area that you have 1 arcana in and beat the withstand. Vs a area W/S spell then all spells (and everything else inside) including the w/s spell within the w/s area gain the addition withstand. Its not till prime 4 when you can dispel all spells in an area easily.<br /> <br /> As has been said already, there will be some points where you dont want to use area spells, esp if your in the area yourself. Sometimes you might just want to dispel x,y,z spells on some threat and leave your own spells active etc etc<br /> <br /> Is it powerful? Yes. Does it need balanced? No. That action your using to dispel things, is one action you arnt using to counter spells being thrown back at you maybe. It'll probably be rare that situations line up perfectly where you'll catch enemy mages in an area and not catch your friends, and who is to say they arnt just going to area dispel all your spells right back at you?<br /> <br /> Mage's are powerful, theres a reason mage society developed consiliums, the duel arcane etc to deal with mage disputes, which basically &quot;balance&quot; mages for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 12-12-2017, 04:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T05:39:26-08:00","id":1166961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1166761-balancing-wards-signs-dispels-supernal-veil?p=1166861#post1166861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man..at least make some effort to present your questions in a readable manner. I'd love to try and help - I'm sure many people would - but you're asking a lot of questions in a nearly incoherent stream of consciousness that makes any attempt at actually sifting through your post for specific questions an exercise in frustration.<br /> <br /> To discuss a couple that I saw mentioned:<br /> <br /> 1) no, you can't dodge or apply Defense against any non-aimed spell, including area spells. Mages don't just always use AOEs because you can't choose the targets of an AOE, it affects all viable subjects in the area indiscriminately, which is often problematic.<br /> 2) No, you can't combine two of the same (or even different) direct damage spells to do double damage, this has been clarified by the devs. Search Dave's posts if you want to find the specific post.<br /> 3) Mudras are part of using a rote, they can't be used independently.<br /> 4) Wards &amp; Signs only applies to awakened magic (spells, attainments, etc). It adds Withstand, a mechanic no system besides Awakened magic even engages with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! Very helpful! 2-4 make perfect sense. I believe firmly that attainments should be withstood by W/S, considering that there are mechanics in place for determining their potency and they presumably are withstood in all other contexts just as their base spells.<br /> <br /> 1 is problematic, though. It means that any mage combat outside of phone booth range can instagib an entire party at first initiative regardless of W/S, barring counterspells. The idea that &quot;it affects all viable targets in the area indiscriminately&quot; applies as much to hand grenades, which my former TFV hunter players are very familiar with. For example, an Adept of Matter could turn all of the air in a small room-sized area into stone/steel/plutonium/acid/lava without so much as a blink from the other side.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11153-bonerstorm","name":"bonerstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T05:53:54-08:00","id":1166965,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s part of the inherent danger of open conflict between Mages, that\u2019s why they avoid it. It\u2019s in fact the exact reason that the Right if Nemesis exists so that if two parties do go into open conflict it won\u2019t spill over and if it does everyone comes after the guy dumb enough to involve bystanders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T05:57:54-08:00","id":1166967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bonerstorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1166761-balancing-wards-signs-dispels-supernal-veil?p=1166961#post1166961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks! Very helpful! 2-4 make perfect sense. I believe firmly that attainments should be withstood by W/S, considering that there are mechanics in place for determining their potency and they presumably are withstood in all other contexts just as their base spells.<br /> <br /> 1 is problematic, though. It means that any mage combat outside of phone booth range can instagib an entire party at first initiative regardless of W/S, barring counterspells. The idea that &quot;it affects all viable targets in the area indiscriminately&quot; applies as much to hand grenades, which my former TFV hunter players are very familiar with. For example, an Adept of Matter could turn all of the air in a small room-sized area into stone/steel/plutonium/acid/lava without so much as a blink from the other side.</div> </div> </div> </div>Once mages hit Adept level, they are borderline unstoppable, especially if they have time to prepare. This is why the game lines do not cross well. Mages in the context of mage alone are fine with Patterning spells, because the game is more about Hubris and investigating whatever strange Mystery lies beyond the room of molten corpses that just died from lava-air. Also the social consequences of that. Mages are often up against Seers of the Throne, or Banishers, or other strange and dangerous creatures who can match their power.<br /> <br /> In a mage game, magic is a tool that lets the mages get through adventures. You can't really stop them from discovering information. They can blast through 99% of a sneaky puzzle with one action thanks to Knowing, Unveiling, and Ruling spells. Mage is a game that doesn't ask &quot;can you do it?&quot; Instead, it asks &quot;<i>should </i>you do it?&quot; Because chances are, yes you can do it.<br /> <br /> You are thinking about the balance in terms of pure combat, which you shouldn't do. Admittedly, this is more of an issue in crossover games than it would be in a pure mage game. The main issue is one player overshadowing the others with magic. Ultimately it comes down to whether or not the players find the game fun. I mean, werewolves can pretty much shred through anything anyway, so combat is probably the least of your worries...<br /> <br /> It really depends on what you plan to do with the mages. If they're going to have some sort of permanent PC role in the game, the group should go into it knowing what mages are capable of and not introducing too many arbitrary limits because lolbalance. Some minor tweaking of the rules is fine, and there have been plenty of topics on this before with lists of suggestions. But more it's about how the players handle the story, I think. It doesn't matter if the mage with Matter can kill everyone in the next room in the blink of an eye... <i>If </i>the group doesn't have a problem with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T06:10:24-08:00","id":1166969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1166761-balancing-wards-signs-dispels-supernal-veil?p=1166927#post1166927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Simple lesson to take from this, Dont cross the streams.<br /> <br /> <br /> Note that unmaking spells are always withstood when used on somebody so no need to house rule it. (though a ES can still ignore the withstand)<br /> <br /> An area dispel magic spell will dispel all spells within the area that you have 1 arcana in and beat the withstand. Vs a area W/S spell then all spells (and everything else inside) including the w/s spell within the w/s area gain the addition withstand. Its not till prime 4 when you can dispel all spells in an area easily.<br /> <br /> As has been said already, there will be some points where you dont want to use area spells, esp if your in the area yourself. Sometimes you might just want to dispel x,y,z spells on some threat and leave your own spells active etc etc<br /> <br /> Is it powerful? Yes. Does it need balanced? No. That action your using to dispel things, is one action you arnt using to counter spells being thrown back at you maybe. It'll probably be rare that situations line up perfectly where you'll catch enemy mages in an area and not catch your friends, and who is to say they arnt just going to area dispel all your spells right back at you?<br /> <br /> Mage's are powerful, theres a reason mage society developed consiliums, the duel arcane etc to deal with mage disputes, which basically &quot;balance&quot; mages for you.</div> </div> </div> </div>By instagib/stunlock, I include &quot;8 aggravated&quot; or &quot;mindwipe indefinite duration&quot; or &quot;spend the next hour doing nothing but chewing your own flesh off&quot; or even &quot;dispelling the spell you are currently using to breathe in the cold vacuum of space&quot; as well as Unmaking practice.<br /> <br /> Your description of area dispels sounds more than a little OP and I can't see it jiving with RAW.<br /> I can't see how &quot;Spells with multiple subjects apply their Potency against the Withstand rating of each individual subject, so may take effect against some of them.&quot; applies to areas. Now that I've had time to think about it, an area dispel would be Withstood jointly by every spell inside that area at a given time. If you want things to be Withstood separately, you have to use subject scale to target the spells separately.<br /> <br /> Example: A mage casts a scene-duration area dispel with potency 10 at a small room. There are 4 active spells in that room, the highest caster Arcana among them being 5. BUT one of the spells was cast at Advanced Potency with caster Arcana 4, so the highest Withstand rating is actually 6. Since they Withstand together for 6 + 1 + 1 + 1, the joint Withstand rating is 9 and the Potency 10 dispel works against all of them. The next point in the initiative somebody else casts any spell that takes effect inside that area, which brings the joint Withstand rating to 10 and disables the dispel... which still counts against spell control. If, on the following turn, that extra spell's duration lapses then the dispel takes effect again.<br /> <br /> Side note: I'd say that you can specify which types of spells an area dispel applies to. Ex: invisibility or supernal veil or specific types of protection spells.<br /> <br /> As for the limiting factor on area dispels and the like being action economy... that really doesn't mean much when Gnosis is a built-in action economy stat. Any mage capable of an area Supernal Dispellation is also capable of combining the spell with an area aggravated Celestial Fire. Again, first initiative TPK instagib.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11153-bonerstorm","name":"bonerstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T06:15:48-08:00","id":1166970,"title":"","content":"If you cast an AoE Dispel then you check its Potency against the Withstand of every spell in the area. If the Potency is higher than the Withstand then the dispel works, if it isn\u2019t then the dispel doesn\u2019t work. It\u2019s pretty straightforward, and works the same way whether you\u2019re using Scale for AoE or number of subjects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T07:10:30-08:00","id":1166983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1166761-balancing-wards-signs-dispels-supernal-veil?p=1166970#post1166970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you cast an AoE Dispel then you check its Potency against the Withstand of every spell in the area. If the Potency is higher than the Withstand then the dispel works, if it isn\u2019t then the dispel doesn\u2019t work. It\u2019s pretty straightforward, and works the same way whether you\u2019re using Scale for AoE or number of subjects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Source?<br /> <br /> Besides being a RAW issue, this is a serious balance issue. If &quot;kill everybody in a small room&quot; was never useful in combat then nobody would have invented grenades. Using AOE to cover a number of subjects you wouldn't be able to Scale Subject target individually means less dice penalty AND you can just chuck the spell instead of spending a reach on Sensory Range.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11153-bonerstorm","name":"bonerstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T07:13:15-08:00","id":1166984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bonerstorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1166761-balancing-wards-signs-dispels-supernal-veil?p=1166983#post1166983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Source?<br /> <br /> Besides being a RAW issue, this is a serious balance issue. If &quot;kill everybody in a small room&quot; was never useful in combat then nobody would have invented grenades. Using AOE to cover a number of subjects you wouldn't be able to Scale Subject target individually means less dice penalty AND you can just chuck the spell instead of spending a reach on Sensory Range.</div> </div> </div> </div>Area spells affect anyone or anything in the target area, as per the spellcasting rules under the Scale factor. You will need Sensory Range unless you want to dispel your own, and probably your cabalmates', spells as well. If you don't use sensory range, the area must be centered on you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T07:15:23-08:00","id":1166986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bonerstorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1166761-balancing-wards-signs-dispels-supernal-veil?p=1166983#post1166983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Source?<br /> <br /> Besides being a RAW issue, this is a serious balance issue. If &amp;quot;kill everybody in a small room&amp;quot; was never useful in combat then nobody would have invented grenades. Using AOE to cover a number of subjects you wouldn't be able to Scale Subject target individually means less dice penalty AND you can just chuck the spell instead of spending a reach on Sensory Range.</div> </div> </div> </div>Source is the rules in the book. I fail to see how it\u2019s a balance issue. If you wish to be indiscriminate you use AoE, if you want to affect multiple specific targets you use number of Subjects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T07:16:08-08:00","id":1166988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bonerstorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1166761-balancing-wards-signs-dispels-supernal-veil?p=1166983#post1166983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Source?<br /> <br /> Besides being a RAW issue, this is a serious balance issue. If &quot;kill everybody in a small room&quot; was never useful in combat then nobody would have invented grenades. Using AOE to cover a number of subjects you wouldn't be able to Scale Subject target individually means less dice penalty AND you can just chuck the spell instead of spending a reach on Sensory Range.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If you cast a Potency 4 AoE dispell-spell in a room with 5 spells, 4 of them being of arcanum 3 and one with 5, the four withstand 3 spells gets dispelled and nothing happens to the last. <br /> This is the same thing as using a spell that forces everyone in the room to comply to your orders with Mind. If one has a higher WS then the potancy, that dude doesnt comply, the others do.<br /> <br /> AoE and spells with mulltiple subjects deal with withstand on a case by case basis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T07:28:29-08:00","id":1166989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1166761-balancing-wards-signs-dispels-supernal-veil?p=1166986#post1166986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Source is the rules in the book. I fail to see how it\u2019s a balance issue. If you wish to be indiscriminate you use AoE, if you want to affect multiple specific targets you use number of Subjects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rules under Scale:<br /> &quot;If using Area of Effect for Scale, the factor instead determines how large the area covered by the spell is, applying the spell effect to anyone or anything within. A mage cannot single out specific subjects in the declared space unless she uses the spell Warding Gesture (see \u201cFate,\u201d p. 136).&quot;<br /> <br /> Rules under Withstanding:<br /> &quot;Spells with multiple subjects apply their Potency against the Withstand rating of each individual subject, so may take effect against some of them. Each spell in a combined spell is Withstood separately. If a spell has multiple Withstand ratings (for example, a Withstood spell cast paradox 115 with the Sympathetic Range Attainment) it uses the highest rating, +1 for every additional rating.&quot;<br /> An AOE spell is not a &quot;spell with multiple subjects.&quot; A spell with multiple subjects is a spell with multiple subje.....<br /> <br /> Unless... an AOE spell is counts anything in the AOE as a &quot;Subject&quot;? That's... extremely powerful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11153-bonerstorm","name":"bonerstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T07:37:26-08:00","id":1166992,"title":"","content":"Yes, AoE considers anything inside its area that could be a viable target for the spell to be one of its subjects.<br /> <br /> Also, yeah, it\u2019s powerful. This is Mage we\u2019re talking about, and I don\u2019t know why you expected it to be any less.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T08:55:52-08:00","id":1167008,"title":"","content":"Dave wrote a good example of area vs targets on the discord:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">(Area) the house is covered by a Potency 3 spell that makes people fall (and stay?) asleep, withstood by resolve. Everyone in the building checks their resolve, one guy with Resolve 4 upstairs is fine, everyone else drops. two women enter, one with Res 2 and one with Res 5. the first drops asleep, the other doesn't. They drag one of the victims out - now outside the spell's Area, they can wake him/them up.<br /> <br /> (Targets) the ten people the Mage can see through the windows are hit by the spell. The dude upstairs wasn't visible (if the mage had maybe scried first, but eh) and doesn't even check, Both women entering the building are fine, but the spell stays on whoever they drag out until its duration runs out.</span></span> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bonerstorm</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless... an AOE spell is counts anything in the AOE as a &quot;Subject&quot;? That's... extremely powerful.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find it weird that you are trying to &quot;balance&quot; anything without having any experience how any of it works in play? Your wanting to nerf things without actually understanding them or having used them, that seems odd.<br /> <br /> You seem worried about &quot;instagib&quot; stuff but what about a long duration ban spell around somebody till they suffocate? Easily done with space 3, hell enough effort and you can ramp that up to campus level and kill everybody inside it eventually. Are you really going to try and think of every clever way mages can overcome something and apply &quot;balance&quot; to it? Or just use it as RAW and accept that using mages as antagonists vs lower powered hunters/werewolfs etc will end badly for the hunter/werewolf side. If the mages arnt antagonists then you just have to accept that they may overshadow the other PC's in certain things. If the mage PC is happy with anything you decide to change then fair enough but personally if i want to play a mage, i want to play a mage, not a &quot;balanced&quot; one just because the mage template does play well with others...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 12-12-2017, 12:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T09:30:33-08:00","id":1167016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1166761-balancing-wards-signs-dispels-supernal-veil?p=1167008#post1167008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dave wrote a good example of area vs targets on the discord:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I find it weird that you are trying to &quot;balance&quot; anything without having any experience how any of it works in play? Your wanting to nerf things without actually understanding them or having used them, that seems odd.<br /> <br /> You seem worried about &quot;instagib&quot; stuff but what about a long duration ban spell around somebody till they suffocate? Easily done with space 3, hell enough effort and you can ramp that up to campus level and kill everybody inside it eventually. Are you really going to try and think of every clever way mages can overcome something and apply &quot;balance&quot; to it? Or just use it as RAW and accept that using mages as antagonists vs lower powered hunters/werewolfs etc will end badly for the hunter/werewolf side. If the mages arnt antagonists then you just have to accept that they may overshadow the other PC's in certain things. If the mage PC is happy with anything you decide to change then fair enough but personally if i want to play a mage, i want to play a mage, not a &quot;balanced&quot; one just because the mage template does play well with others...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I dig. Ban was also one of those spells I wanted to find a way around.<br /> <br /> So... does this mean that, say, a scene-duration campus area dispel of high enough potency or with exceptional success ignore withstand would suppress every single spell in the entire area? Even after casting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11153-bonerstorm","name":"bonerstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T09:49:03-08:00","id":1167018,"title":"","content":"There we go! That's how you balance mage: AOE praxis dispel so there are no spells. No spells, no problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11153-bonerstorm","name":"bonerstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T09:49:44-08:00","id":1167019,"title":"","content":"Yeah, though if you really wanted to target all spells you\u2019d be better off using the Prime 4 version that doesn\u2019t have additional arcana prerequisites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T10:03:06-08:00","id":1167026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1166761-balancing-wards-signs-dispels-supernal-veil?p=1167019#post1167019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, though if you really wanted to target all spells you\u2019d be better off using the Prime 4 version that doesn\u2019t have additional arcana prerequisites.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1D2129\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">But would a dispel dispel an area dispel or would the area dispel dispel that dispel before it could be dispelled?</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11153-bonerstorm","name":"bonerstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T10:03:33-08:00","id":1167027,"title":"","content":"Also, pro tip: when multiple people tell you that something is already in the rules, don't be so certain that you know it isn't. Makes it look like you didn't actually read them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T10:05:20-08:00","id":1167028,"title":"","content":"I guess it'd have to be a BIGGER area dispel to dispel the area dispel so it doesn't dispel the area dispel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11153-bonerstorm","name":"bonerstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T10:07:59-08:00","id":1167032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>arthexis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1166761-balancing-wards-signs-dispels-supernal-veil?p=1167027#post1167027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, pro tip: when multiple people tell you that something is already in the rules, don't be so certain that you know it isn't. Makes it look like you didn't actually read them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, pardon me, but the rules aren't exactly clear about subjects vs AOE, especially considering most of the rules about them lay them out as mutually exclusive. And, point of fact, I have read the rules and there is nothing that explicitly says that everything inside an AOE is treated as a separate subject per separate subject rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11153-bonerstorm","name":"bonerstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T10:16:37-08:00","id":1167036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bonerstorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1166761-balancing-wards-signs-dispels-supernal-veil?p=1167026#post1167026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exactly!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1D2129\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">But would a dispel dispel an area dispel or would the area dispel dispel that dispel before it could be dispelled?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I assume the dispel spell will dispel itself since it is also in its area but with the +2 lasting reach though this isnt much a problem if every spell is gone and not just suppressed. Without the lasting reach this is the problem i had coming up with a potency 6 long duration dispel magic anti area effect spell but adding the fate 1 option to selectively ignore the dispel spell ie itself solves that problem. (if it didnt have that fate option you could combine cast it with warding gesture to ignore itself)<br /> <br /> So yes, a potency 6 campus sized supernal dispellation spell using the fate 1 option to ignore itself, creates an area where any spell entering or cast inside it gets suppressed but somebody can just dispel the supernal dispellation spell.<br /> <br /> Not quite sure how this interacts with instant duration spells though, i think it doesnt work on them as they would be over by the time the dispel gets to act? You really need to counterspell those as they are gone well before dispel is viable...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 12-12-2017, 01:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T10:41:49-08:00","id":1167041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1166761-balancing-wards-signs-dispels-supernal-veil?p=1167036#post1167036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I assume the dispel spell will dispel itself since it is also in its area but with the +2 lasting reach though this isnt much a problem if every spell is gone and not just suppressed. Without the lasting reach this is the problem i had coming up with a potency 6 long duration dispel magic anti area effect spell but adding the fate 1 option to selectively ignore the dispel spell ie itself solves that problem. (if it didnt have that fate option you could combine cast it with warding gesture to ignore itself)<br /> <br /> So yes, a potency 6 campus sized supernal dispellation spell using the fate 1 option to ignore itself, creates an area where any spell entering or cast inside it gets suppressed but somebody can just dispel the supernal dispellation spell.<br /> <br /> Not quite sure how this interacts with instant duration spells though, i think it doesnt work on them as they would be over by the time the dispel gets to act? You really need to counterspell those as they are gone well before dispel is viable...</div> </div> </div> </div>But if an area dispel dispels itself then won't that dispel its dispelling of itself? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also there are no instant duration spells in MTAw. Every spell is minimum 1 turn, which is why multiple reflexive spells count towards spell control.<br /> <br /> If I weren't just being a jerk poking fun at the rules, I'd say that a dispel of a dispel provokes a COW and the loser is suppressed for the duration of the winner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11153-bonerstorm","name":"bonerstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T11:02:45-08:00","id":1167050,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I don't think a spell can target itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T11:45:46-08:00","id":1167063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bonerstorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1166761-balancing-wards-signs-dispels-supernal-veil?p=1167041#post1167041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if an area dispel dispels itself then won't that dispel its dispelling of itself? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also there are no instant duration spells in MTAw. Every spell is minimum 1 turn, which is why multiple reflexive spells count towards spell control.<br /> <br /> If I weren't just being a jerk poking fun at the rules, I'd say that a dispel of a dispel provokes a COW and the loser is suppressed for the duration of the winner.</div> </div> </div> </div>A spell that only lasts 3 seconds lasts for a instant. The same length a instant action takes. Hence a instant duration spell. It takes a instant to cast and lasts a a instant.<br /> <br /> No, a person can just dispel the supernal dispellation spell as if it were any other spell. Theres nothing about the dispel magic or supernal dispellation spell that makes them different from other spells when attempting to dispel them. Layer 2 area dispels over each other and the one with the higher potency wins as usual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 12-12-2017, 02:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T12:29:00-08:00","id":1167077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bonerstorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1166761-balancing-wards-signs-dispels-supernal-veil?p=1166961#post1166961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, an Adept of Matter could turn all of the air in a small room-sized area into stone/steel/plutonium/acid/lava without so much as a blink from the other side.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct.<br /> That's not even half as dangerous as what a well-built starting Mastigos can do.<br /> <br /> Your question was 'why don't they do it all the time' and the answer is 'because there are times where collateral damage is undesirable'. I've played and run a lot (hundreds of hours) of 2E Mage. I can count the number of times I was in a situation where indiscriminate AOE hostile magic was a good idea on one hand. Unless you're running some weird D&amp;D in ChroD dungeon crawl thing (or some kind of military sim? idk), it's not really common. If you are, I could see why that might be problematic.<br /> <br /> Widely scaled magic is much more dangerous and common when they are beneficial spells targeting the party, because generally speaking, most mages can easily find situations where they can perfectly control <i>who</i> is present to receive the benefit of their magic, and stack much higher dice modifiers for it with no fear of Paradox (by using a Demesne). <br /> <br /> It is harder to control the circumstances where hostile magic is applied, because it is less likely to be applied on home turf and more likely to be applied in chaotic situations.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T12:29:47-08:00","id":1167078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1166761-balancing-wards-signs-dispels-supernal-veil?p=1167063#post1167063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A spell that only lasts 3 seconds lasts for a instant. The same length a instant action takes. Hence a instant duration spell. It takes a instant to cast and lasts a a instant.<br /> <br /> No, a person can just dispel the supernal dispellation spell as if it were any other spell. Theres nothing about the dispel magic or supernal dispellation spell that makes them different from other spells when attempting to dispel them. Layer 2 area dispels over each other and the one with the higher potency wins as usual.</div> </div> </div> </div>But does the dispel dispel the dispel or does the dispel dispel the dispel? There's no ordering of spell effects in MTAw, so they take effect simultaneously: the original dispel suppresses the dispel that suppresses it. That's why I say, practically, dispelling an area dispel should be dealt with by clash of wills because they can't suppress each others' effects without nullifying said suppression. Using the reach for Lasting duration would be effectively equivalent to indefinite duration = +4 bonus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11153-bonerstorm","name":"bonerstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T12:34:18-08:00","id":1167080,"title":"","content":"Just because a spell's duration minimum is one turn doesn't actually mean that the spell lasts for an entire turn. A dispel takes effect immediately, and there's no further effect for another dispel to fight against.<br /> <br /> I believe Dave clarified this somewhere (that not all spells linger for a full turn), though that was in relation to damage spells, iirc. I can't find the post now, or I would link it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 12-12-2017, 03:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T12:36:03-08:00","id":1167082,"title":"","content":"Dispel is transitory. Also, Dispel is not a counterspell. It only affects ongoing spells with non-transitory durations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T12:40:42-08:00","id":1167084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1166761-balancing-wards-signs-dispels-supernal-veil?p=1167077#post1167077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correct.<br /> That's not even half as dangerous as what a well-built starting Mastigos can do.<br /> <br /> Your question was 'why don't they do it all the time' and the answer is 'because there are times where collateral damage is undesirable'. I've played and run a lot (hundreds of hours) of 2E Mage. I can count the number of times I was in a situation where indiscriminate AOE hostile magic was a good idea on one hand. Unless you're running some weird D&amp;D in ChroD dungeon crawl thing (or some kind of military sim? idk), it's not really common. If you are, I could see why that might be problematic.<br /> <br /> Widely scaled magic is much more dangerous and common when they are beneficial spells targeting the party, because generally speaking, most mages can easily find situations where they can perfectly control <i>who</i> is present to receive the benefit of their magic, and stack much higher dice modifiers for it with no fear of Paradox (by using a Demesne).<br /> <br /> It is harder to control the circumstances where hostile magic is applied, because it is less likely to be applied on home turf and more likely to be applied in chaotic situations.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>True enough. That said, I'm about to put my players through an Atlantean dungeon/temple/thing which is theoretically a part of Mage gameplay so... yeah. I guess I could be like &quot;ohh noo you don't want to upset the delicate magical balance of wards and blah blah&quot; but there are limits to that.<br /> <br /> Regardless, MTAw feels so much like incredible rocket tag that... I'm struggling to see how this can be fun. I know my players and I know they will kill literally everything everywhere all the time. They're playing Werewolf now and had played Hunter before that so it goes with the territory. Conversely, they know I won't pull punches so I'm trying to imagine a scenario where I don't just kill them all or they don't just kill my NPC demilich on the first point in the initiative.<br /> <br /> Specifically: There are a multitude of powers that instagib. There are few powers that protect, and those can be easily bypassed. Literally nothing can stop a 1st initiative praxis nuke exceptional from one of the Arcana that doesn't have a COW shield.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11153-bonerstorm","name":"bonerstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T12:43:35-08:00","id":1167085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bonerstorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1166761-balancing-wards-signs-dispels-supernal-veil?p=1167084#post1167084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regardless, MTAw feels so much like incredible rocket tag that... I'm struggling to see how this can be fun. I know my players and I know they will kill literally everything everywhere all the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then they won't last very long if you're playing a setting consistent with what's present in the books, because those much more powerful and experienced than them are not going to let that shit slide. <br /> <br /> The entirety of Mage society is a check &amp; balance against this kind of behavior.<br /> <br /> When everyone has a nuke, you learn how to be conservative with using your own, or <i>everyone else points theirs at you.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T12:44:37-08:00","id":1167087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>arthexis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1166761-balancing-wards-signs-dispels-supernal-veil?p=1167082#post1167082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dispel is transitory. Also, Dispel is not a counterspell. It only affects ongoing spells with non-transitory durations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Transitory = Standard Duration in 2E. Basic success Transitory duration is 1 Turn. If an area Dispel affects every spell in the area, it affects spells with Duration of 1 turn. There is no such thing as completely instantaneous casting in 2E unless you define &quot;instantaneous&quot; as 1 Turn. Look it up and tell me if I'm wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11153-bonerstorm","name":"bonerstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T12:46:50-08:00","id":1167090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1166761-balancing-wards-signs-dispels-supernal-veil?p=1167085#post1167085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then they won't last very long if you're playing a setting consistent with what's present in the books, because those much more powerful and experienced than them are not going to let that shit slide.<br /> <br /> The entirety of Mage society is a check &amp; balance against this kind of behavior.<br /> <br /> When everyone has a nuke, you learn how to be conservative with using your own, or <i>everyone else points theirs at you.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>But what about Banishers and Scelesti and Reapers? Do they politely introduce themselves and challenge their opponents to an Arcane Duel?<br /> <br /> Everyone is a minor god = powers don't matter = combat isn't really supposed to happen anyway = 1st initiative always wins = magical nuclear tea party = why bother?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11153-bonerstorm","name":"bonerstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T12:49:03-08:00","id":1167092,"title":"","content":"Casting the spell takes a turn. The effects of some spells can be completely instantaneous or at least shorter than 3 seconds. If I smack something with Telekinesis, it receives the whole impact over a period of time that has the be smaller than 3 seconds, or its going to be a completely ineffective attack. Don't just rely on the literal words in the book, you have to interpret a text for it to make sense, and reading it like you do makes no sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T12:51:38-08:00","id":1167094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bonerstorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1166761-balancing-wards-signs-dispels-supernal-veil?p=1167090#post1167090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But what about Banishers and Scelesti and Reapers? Do they politely introduce themselves and challenge their opponents to an Arcane Duel?</div> </div> </div> </div>If one of them shows up that is on an equal power level with PCs, the story that should be getting told is how each party prepares to seize the advantage in the inevitable confrontation, not how they ran headlong into each other hoping for a lucky diceroll when their lives and the lives of their compatriots were on the line.<br /> <br /> None of the things you've mentioned are D&amp;D monsters that exist to die to the adventurers. They all generally want to continue living just as badly as the PCs, and will be fully aware that a head to head confrontation is likely not in their favor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bonerstorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1166761-balancing-wards-signs-dispels-supernal-veil?p=1167090#post1167090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everyone is a minor god = powers don't matter = combat isn't really supposed to happen anyway = 1st initiative always wins = magical nuclear tea party = why bother?</div> </div> </div> </div>It kind of sounds like this might not be the type of game you would enjoy, yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T12:57:04-08:00","id":1167096,"title":"","content":"I mean if you -must- have combat, use stuff from the Abyss, or the Bound, or rank 6 entities, other Mages won't really do for a &quot;typical&quot; engagement unless they've entered some pre-arranged agreement for how matters will be settled, and you trust them not to cheat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 12-12-2017, 04:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T13:01:19-08:00","id":1167098,"title":"","content":"Don't get me wrong - combat has happened a <i>lot</i> in my games. Rarely, it's mage-on-mage. But every single time that happens, every party involved understands that going for blood is probably a bad idea, and if they decide to do so, a single unlucky diceroll probably means that they no longer exist.<br /> <br /> If your question is 'Can I have traditional turn-by-turn combat in a game where a starting character can telepathically order an entire neighborhood to kill themselves and likely succeed, or turn air into fissile material that can detonate into a legitimate nuclear explosion' then the answer is no.<br /> <br /> You could make changes to make that possible, but they would have to be so sweeping you would no longer be playing Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T13:33:53-08:00","id":1167107,"title":"","content":"Also, I play Mage for the philosophy. We tend to have a lot of fun debates around the table that we don't always have with, say, D&amp;D. (Not to disparage D&amp;D, I love 5th edition). <br /> <br /> I agree that it also means that maybe not everyone wants to play Mage all the time because it requires more work than other games from everyone. And that's fine. I am one that thinks the complexity of 2e should be toned down a notch, but not entirely and certainly not in the sake of balance. <br /> <br /> Typically what I do when other supernaturals show up in my mage game is that I decide if they are a challenge or not, up front. If I want them to be a challenge I think a number of things that will create that challenge, beyond just stats.<br /> <br /> For example, in one of my games, a pair of mages were investigating a Sleeper and discovered she was turned into a Vampire. They didn't know enough about vampires and tried to shadow one to learn more. This eventually lead to combat, for which they were not well prepared. The mages completely obliterated him but took some claws to the ribs in the process. In another scene, they interrogated a Vampire by holding him in place with Space and letting him know they could keep him there until sunrise. But these vampires were not &quot;challenges&quot; they are just small speed bumps (and a way to allow the players to better explore the setting). <br /> <br /> The real challenge came when an Ordo Dracul Ventrue Elder had designed a Scale to travel the Astral in torpor and kept spying on their secrets (and Dominating their Astral forms) while developing another Scale that turned Sleepwalkers into hosts of Abyssal intruders. Also, they needed the help of this vampire to retrieve something the Concilium had taken from them. And because he was a potential ally against a large-scale confrontation between vampires and mages that may or may not have been caused by Concilium officials and/or Strix. Also, their constant meddling with vampires helped the Kindred locate their sanctum (which made them risk the safety of their retainers, and this after they had to leave their previous sanctum due to certain activities that attracted werewolves). You will need more than combat spells to untangle that one (unless the solution is destroying the city). It was fun!<br /> <br /> So, now that I think about it, Mage is a great game if you like convoluted storylines and combing through weird situations like I do. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T13:46:32-08:00","id":1167115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1166761-balancing-wards-signs-dispels-supernal-veil?p=1167098#post1167098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't get me wrong - combat has happened a <i>lot</i> in my games. Rarely, it's mage-on-mage. But every single time that happens, every party involved understands that going for blood is probably a bad idea, and if they decide to do so, a single unlucky diceroll probably means that they no longer exist.<br /> <br /> If your question is 'Can I have traditional turn-by-turn combat in a game where a starting character can telepathically order an entire neighborhood to kill themselves and likely succeed, or turn air into fissile material that can detonate into a legitimate nuclear explosion' then the answer is no.<br /> <br /> You could make changes to make that possible, but they would have to be so sweeping you would no longer be playing Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">I mean if you -must- have combat, use stuff from the Abyss, or the Bound, or rank 6 entities, other Mages won't really do for a &quot;typical&quot; engagement unless they've entered some pre-arranged agreement for how matters will be settled, and you trust them not to cheat.</span></div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <br /> These are both helpful points.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11153-bonerstorm","name":"bonerstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T13:55:06-08:00","id":1167119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>arthexis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1166761-balancing-wards-signs-dispels-supernal-veil?p=1167092#post1167092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Casting the spell takes a turn. The effects of some spells can be completely instantaneous or at least shorter than 3 seconds. If I smack something with Telekinesis, it receives the whole impact over a period of time that has the be smaller than 3 seconds, or its going to be a completely ineffective attack. Don't just rely on the literal words in the book, you have to interpret a text for it to make sense, and reading it like you do makes no sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Regardless, the spell stays in spell control for a minimum of 3 seconds. Even if it didn't, an area dispel that suppresses all magic inside the area.... suppresses all magic inside the area. Nowhere in 2E is there a definition for transitory magic that is not subject to a dispel. An area dispel is basically an antimagic field. You can cast as many spells as you like and throw them wherever you want... but they won't take effect inside that area unless the withstand rating of your spell is greater than the dispel's potency.<br /> <br /> So telekinesis or levitation is a magical force exerted on an object. The object is not necessarily magical, but the force is. If the force is dispelled, there's no intertia. The rules are unclear but that's the way things like Velocity Control read.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11153-bonerstorm","name":"bonerstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T14:06:20-08:00","id":1167123,"title":"","content":"Besides, Creative Thaumaturgy means you can create a new Dispel Magic that affects Transitory spells anyway. You can also make a COW shield for any Arcana too. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T14:12:52-08:00","id":1167127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bonerstorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1166761-balancing-wards-signs-dispels-supernal-veil?p=1167119#post1167119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regardless, the spell stays in spell control for a minimum of 3 seconds. Even if it didn't, an area dispel that suppresses all magic inside the area.... suppresses all magic inside the area. Nowhere in 2E is there a definition for transitory magic that is not subject to a dispel. An area dispel is basically an antimagic field. You can cast as many spells as you like and throw them wherever you want... but they won't take effect inside that area unless the withstand rating of your spell is greater than the dispel's potency.<br /> <br /> So telekinesis or levitation is a magical force exerted on an object. The object is not necessarily magical, but the force is. If the force is dispelled, there's no intertia. The rules are unclear but that's the way things like Velocity Control read.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wait, i think you are confused. A area sized transitory duration supernal dispellation spell will suppress all spells inside its area for its duration of 1 turn. Which probably isnt that useful, unless you just need to bypass a ban to let others past it or something or use the lasting reach. A supernal dispellation spell with a longer duration will suppress all the spells insides its area for the supernal dispellation spells duration or until somebody else dispells that spell.<br /> <br /> Spells of transitory duration can either a) still be cast inside the supernal dispellation spells area because they are over before the supernal dispelation spell can take effect OR b) the transitory spell fails to cast as it gets dispelled the moment it appears in the fallen realm so quickly it cant take effect.<br /> <br /> You cant normally dispel a transitory spell because its over before you can target it with your dispel spell which is why there is counterspell.<br /> <br /> I suppose if you had a zone of control fire that had enough potency to lower all fires started within it to lower than 1 so they got extinguished then the same should apply for spells, you try starting a spell inside the supernal dispellation zone and it gets suppressed for its 3 second duration and then expires. Hence B seems the correct option","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 12-12-2017, 05:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T14:13:36-08:00","id":1167128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1166761-balancing-wards-signs-dispels-supernal-veil?p=1167123#post1167123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides, Creative Thaumaturgy means you can create a new Dispel Magic that affects Transitory spells anyway. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That would completely negate the point of counterspell, so no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T16:45:20-08:00","id":1167182,"title":"","content":"I had mage on mage combat in my game tonight (versus Banishers). The city was under attack by a Banisher plague, and the general &quot;kill 'em all&quot; order went out.<br /> <br /> One of the Banishers had Life 5 and Death 5. I did stay away from the Unmaking spells, but I was able to deal 8 Lethal damage and cause the Immobilized tilt by setting one of the PC's nerves on (metaphorical) fire. There were a lot of Patterning spells flung around, though. Chaos Mastery is the bane of my existence. Things were complicated by the Abyssal Environmental Tilt one of the PCs caused. She used an artifact that cast Reshaping to make a giant hole in order to trap the Banishers. Except she was Rampant, and the Artifact pulled in too much Paradox.<br /> <br /> So, this resulted in a flood of constantly replicating crystals that screamed and shattered repeatedly, creating a fine silver dust cloud that increased Paradox dice pools and cut at the skin. All of this was contained in a Ban. Fun! The Banishers' first move was to Sever the Awakened Soul, but that didn't go so well thanks to a Shielding spell the players had. This fight ended with one PC using Abyssal spellcasting to close the hole to the Abyss, and another PC getting outted as a Tremere when he refused to return the soul that he had severed in order to neutralize one of the Banishers.<br /> <br /> I think my cabal is easily falling into line as a bunch of self-serving psychopaths that perform good deeds as collateral damage...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-13T13:51:19-08:00","id":1167405,"title":"","content":"Mage on Mage combat seems to be a dish best served sparingly, but it can definitely be fun. I tend not to play my NPCs 'optimally' or whatever, because they are flawed human beings, much like the PC's (who themselves usually make a mess of things.) The trick to making it all worthwhile is to have some kind of interesting 3rd (or 4th) element to the scene beyond the simple fact of a confrontation. Perhaps the clash is happening in a crowded street, forcing the PC's to consider Wisdom, Paradox and the potential of dozens of innocent casualties while their Scelestus antagonist cares for none of these things. <br /> <br /> Perhaps the 'Mage' they are fighting is actually a helpless Sleeper possessed by a Seer using a Profane Urim. Then the question isn't 'can they defeat him' its 'how much are they willing to risk to save this man.'<br /> <br /> As has been stated, Mages are capable of a great deal. That means the challenges you throw at them have to be quite hefty too, don't be afraid of chucking in moral conundrums or odd requests, working out an elegant solution to such things is half the fun of the game. <br /> <br /> For example, in a Halloween themed session a few weeks back, my Moros and Obrimos PC's had to work together to gather a laundry list of items for a unique ritual (otherwise the Iris in the basement of their house was going to condemn all of southern England to a new Ice Age, but thats another story.) This list included.<ul><li>The skull of a murderer, the blood of a victim.</li> <li>A sliver of captured moonlight, a newborn bird that has only seen one dawn.</li> <li>The ashes of an ardent love letter, and the written bile of a man consumed by hate</li> </ul>I had only faint outlines as to how they would achieve this, but the proceeding couple of hours worth of scenes where they worked out various schemes to gather the reagents was a blast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T08:40:17-08:00","id":1167648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1166761-balancing-wards-signs-dispels-supernal-veil?p=1167127#post1167127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Wait, i think you are confused. A area sized transitory duration supernal dispellation spell will suppress all spells inside its area for its duration of 1 turn. Which probably isnt that useful, unless you just need to bypass a ban to let others past it or something or use the lasting reach. A supernal dispellation spell with a longer duration will suppress all the spells insides its area for the supernal dispellation spells duration or until somebody else dispells that spell.<br /> <br /> Spells of transitory duration can either a) still be cast inside the supernal dispellation spells area because they are over before the supernal dispelation spell can take effect OR b) the transitory spell fails to cast as it gets dispelled the moment it appears in the fallen realm so quickly it cant take effect.<br /> <br /> You cant normally dispel a transitory spell because its over before you can target it with your dispel spell which is why there is counterspell.<br /> <br /> I suppose if you had a zone of control fire that had enough potency to lower all fires started within it to lower than 1 so they got extinguished then the same should apply for spells, you try starting a spell inside the supernal dispellation zone and it gets suppressed for its 3 second duration and then expires. Hence B seems the correct option</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're missing the point: There is no such thing as instantaneous transitory spells in 2e so there's no such thing as a spell that wouldn't be suppressed by an AOE dispel during the AOE dispel's duration. In 2E, &quot;transitory&quot; means spells without Advanced Duration... of which the minimum &quot;transitory&quot; duration is 1 turn.<br /> <br /> Example with Thyrsus Mage 1 and Obrimos Mage 2:<br /> Mage 1 has Potency 20 W/S up from his buddy with lots of time on his hands and Prime Arcana 4. Mage 2's initiative comes up first and they cast an Advanced Scale area combined praxis spell of Celestial Fire and Supernal Dispellation with a reach for Aggravated damage at Mage 1; the spell has a potency of 7 and a minimum duration of 1 turn and Mage 1 gets an exceptional success with a roll of 3, opting to ignore Withstands.<br /> <br /> Mage 2 uses 4 Mana to power the 2 Reach and doesn't need to use Sensory Range because he can just chuck the spell with an attack roll of Gnosis + Firearms/Athletics. With Fast Spells, Mage 1 could only apply defense to a chucked spell if they could apply defense to bullets; even if they could, they can't apply defense to or dodge an area spell anyway. Just for giggles, because Mage 2 has Fate 1, they specify that it will only suppress spells that don't hurt Mage 2.<br /> <br /> Mage 1 can't dodge this and, of course, can't counterspell it without Prime magic. His withstand of the CF from Potency 20 W/S is ignored because it's an area spell. Even if it didn't, it would be ignored because of the exceptional success. Even if it didn't, the Supernal Dispellation beats any Withstand of W/S. Even if it didn't, the Potency of 7 means it would dispel W/S even if it had been cast with Advanced Potency. Even if W/S was somehow from an attainment and thus couldn't be dispelled, its withstand rating would be ignored by Celestial Fire because of the exceptional success.<br /> <br /> So Mage 1 is in a &quot;large house or building&quot; sized area in which all spells are subject to ignores-withstand Supernal Dispellation and everything is subject to 7 points of aggravated from Celestial Fire (including beings in Twilight). Arguably neither his Spirit Armor nor Life Armor apply against this damage. Thankfully, Mage 1 has Life 4 and Mend as a rote so they cast Mend with a reach to heal aggravated damage... unfortunately the area dispel is still in effect and nullifies Mend because it is within the area during the duration (1 turn). The Supernal Dispellation would nullify ANY non-archmage spell because of the ignoring of withstands from exceptional success and, even if the Storyteller houseruled against that, Mend's Withstand wouldn't beat SupDisp's Potency of 7 even with Advanced Potency.<br /> <br /> Mage 1's player says: &quot;But wait! Mend is a transitory spell! It takes effect instantly and can't be dispelled.&quot; The Storyteller says: &quot;That is literally not what Transitory means. If you look at the rulebook, transitory just means it doesn't have Advanced Duration. The only reference to 'immediate' effects are on page 113 in a section saying what happens when a heal or damage spell etc is cast with an extended duration. If the spell takes effect immediately, it still gets dispelled immediately. The book does not say what you say it does.&quot;<br /> <br /> Supernal Dispellation:<br /> &quot;Supernal truths can never truly be unmade, but with this spell<br /> the mage may cast them back across the Abyss, effectively erasing<br /> any spell she comes across. This spell is not potent enough to<br /> dispel archmages\u2019 spells.<br /> A successful casting suppresses the spell for the Duration of<br /> Supernal Dispellation.&quot;<br /> <br /> If an area spell treats all possible subjects within its area as its subject which each withstands separately, then it suppresses every spell cast in the area during its duration. Period. The only way for Mage 1 to escape Mage 2's spell is to escape the &quot;large house or building&quot; sized area if their Speed allows.<br /> <br /> This is why I think area spells treating everything within AOE as subject, which is otherwise limited, is bats*** f****** insane. If it's RAW, that's cool. Still insanely OP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11153-bonerstorm","name":"bonerstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T08:55:49-08:00","id":1167659,"title":"","content":"Random fun thoughts:<br /> <br /> 1) Prime 2: Un-Wards and Un-Signs Withstands any benign magic cast on the subject.<br /> <br /> 2) An extended duration area Psychic Domination to &quot;kill yourself with the most convenient pointy object in the room&quot; would work on anyone who entered the area during the duration. HOWEVER, if the command was &quot;go to 7-11 and buy Billy Bob pack of smokes&quot; it would fail the moment people left the area... since then they would no longer be subjects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11153-bonerstorm","name":"bonerstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T09:11:26-08:00","id":1167670,"title":"","content":"1) Wouldn\u2019t work unless it forced the subject of the spell to use their Withstand as Withstand can be voluntarily waived and that\u2019s the default of approach of someone being targeted by a benign spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T10:56:28-08:00","id":1167709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bonerstorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1166761-balancing-wards-signs-dispels-supernal-veil?p=1167648#post1167648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you're missing the point: There is no such thing as instantaneous transitory spells in 2e so there's no such thing as a spell that wouldn't be suppressed by an AOE dispel during the AOE dispel's duration. In 2E, &quot;transitory&quot; means spells without Advanced Duration... of which the minimum &quot;transitory&quot; duration is 1 turn.<br /> <br /> Example with Thyrsus Mage 1 and Obrimos Mage 2:<br /> Mage 1 has Potency 20 W/S up from his buddy with lots of time on his hands and Prime Arcana 4. Mage 2's initiative comes up first and they cast an Advanced Scale area combined praxis spell of Celestial Fire and Supernal Dispellation with a reach for Aggravated damage at Mage 1; the spell has a potency of 7 and a minimum duration of 1 turn and Mage 1 gets an exceptional success with a roll of 3, opting to ignore Withstands.<br /> <br /> Mage 2 uses 4 Mana to power the 2 Reach and doesn't need to use Sensory Range because he can just chuck the spell with an attack roll of Gnosis + Firearms/Athletics. With Fast Spells, Mage 1 could only apply defense to a chucked spell if they could apply defense to bullets; even if they could, they can't apply defense to or dodge an area spell anyway. Just for giggles, because Mage 2 has Fate 1, they specify that it will only suppress spells that don't hurt Mage 2.<br /> <br /> Mage 1 can't dodge this and, of course, can't counterspell it without Prime magic. His withstand of the CF from Potency 20 W/S is ignored because it's an area spell. Even if it didn't, it would be ignored because of the exceptional success. Even if it didn't, the Supernal Dispellation beats any Withstand of W/S. Even if it didn't, the Potency of 7 means it would dispel W/S even if it had been cast with Advanced Potency. Even if W/S was somehow from an attainment and thus couldn't be dispelled, its withstand rating would be ignored by Celestial Fire because of the exceptional success.<br /> <br /> So Mage 1 is in a &quot;large house or building&quot; sized area in which all spells are subject to ignores-withstand Supernal Dispellation and everything is subject to 7 points of aggravated from Celestial Fire (including beings in Twilight). Arguably neither his Spirit Armor nor Life Armor apply against this damage. Thankfully, Mage 1 has Life 4 and Mend as a rote so they cast Mend with a reach to heal aggravated damage... unfortunately the area dispel is still in effect and nullifies Mend because it is within the area during the duration (1 turn). The Supernal Dispellation would nullify ANY non-archmage spell because of the ignoring of withstands from exceptional success and, even if the Storyteller houseruled against that, Mend's Withstand wouldn't beat SupDisp's Potency of 7 even with Advanced Potency.<br /> <br /> Mage 1's player says: &quot;But wait! Mend is a transitory spell! It takes effect instantly and can't be dispelled.&quot; The Storyteller says: &quot;That is literally not what Transitory means. If you look at the rulebook, transitory just means it doesn't have Advanced Duration. The only reference to 'immediate' effects are on page 113 in a section saying what happens when a heal or damage spell etc is cast with an extended duration. If the spell takes effect immediately, it still gets dispelled immediately. The book does not say what you say it does.&quot;<br /> <br /> Supernal Dispellation:<br /> &quot;Supernal truths can never truly be unmade, but with this spell<br /> the mage may cast them back across the Abyss, effectively erasing<br /> any spell she comes across. This spell is not potent enough to<br /> dispel archmages\u2019 spells.<br /> A successful casting suppresses the spell for the Duration of<br /> Supernal Dispellation.&quot;<br /> <br /> If an area spell treats all possible subjects within its area as its subject which each withstands separately, then it suppresses every spell cast in the area during its duration. Period. The only way for Mage 1 to escape Mage 2's spell is to escape the &quot;large house or building&quot; sized area if their Speed allows.<br /> <br /> This is why I think area spells treating everything within AOE as subject, which is otherwise limited, is bats*** f****** insane. If it's RAW, that's cool. Still insanely OP.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Supernal Dispellation's primary factor is Potency, like an attack spell. Attack spells pulse when you pump their Duration and reoccur at intervals relative to your Gnosis.<br /> <br /> With 2+ Reach you could destroy any spells you catch on the initial casting, but people could cast other stuff in the mean time. The spell does not say it continuously suppresses all new attempts to cast spells. It merely states that ongoing spells, upon successful casting of Supernal Dispellation, are suppressed for the Duration of Supernal Dispellation - which is by default 1 turn (or 3 seconds). If you switch it to Advanced Duration, you simply extend the interval at which your spell will ping off and capture new spells by an interval designated by your Gnosis.<br /> <br /> A casting of Supernal Dispellation with Advanced Duration at Gnosis 10 would go off every 20 turns and capture any non-archmage spells in its radius at that interval.<br /> <br /> My reason for reading it this way is the inherent reason for why Duration and Potency are not supposed to be arbitrarily decided. The intent of Supernal Dispellation is to suppress magic happening at the time of its casting.<br /> <br /> If we're going RAW, it says nothing about intervening in any new spells. It explicitly refers to what is already on the plate. This is why you've been told that Counterspell is more effective for real time dispellation because it counters the spell live, no matter if its duration is 1 turn or 1 year. It happens in the moment.<br /> <br /> Supernal Dispellation would only work against the spells on the plate, then you would need to wait to snag any future spells that are cast with durations that meet with another interval of Supernal Dispellation. In the meantime, you would still need to use Counterspell to mess with any new spells, especially if they only exist for long enough to do what they need to do and then end before your Supernal Dispellation interval comes up.<br /> <br /> Mage 1 would be free to cast Mend. However, if Mend is cast with a long Duration, and that Duration crosses the next interval of Supernal Dispellation while still being in its radius, Mend is suppressed.<br /> <br /> So the Mage is better off keeping it short and sweet, or dispelling your Supernal Dispellation as soon as possible. Or just leaving the area.<br /> <br /> Supernal Dispellation seems like it matters more outside of combat than in the fray. Granted, you could probably use Time or Fate to get it to do what you're trying to do with it (aka go off every turn or go off specifically when new spells are cast).<br /> <br /> RAW &quot;effectively erasing any spell she comes across&quot; is disingenuous because spells are not erased unless the Reach cost is paid. &quot;A successful casting suppresses the spell for the Duration of Supernal Dispellation&quot; sounds like it makes more sense within the context of addressing ongoing phenomenon at the time of casting, not all phenomenon that will be cast.<br /> <br /> You can read it that way and get an overpowered reading, or you could bring it back (while acknowledging it says nothing about suppressing all new spells as they arise in real time within the vicinity) and give it a more reasonable Heal/Damage spell reading - again, on the basis that it is a Potency spell. Read it as though you've cast an AoE healing or damage spell.<br /> <br /> If the solution is to &quot;balance&quot; it, then all it takes is to read it within the context of primary factor and spells like it. If your only interpretation is to give it the most broken effect based on words that are explicitly not stated, then I don't know what to tell you. Sometimes the stuff written in the book doesn't match what was meant exactly. In those cases we have to read the spell with the context and spirit of the game and hopefully come out on the other side with something workable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">N/A</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","name":"kryptonitekrusher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T11:10:35-08:00","id":1167713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bonerstorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1166761-balancing-wards-signs-dispels-supernal-veil?p=1167648#post1167648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you're missing the point: There is no such thing as instantaneous transitory spells in 2e so there's no such thing as a spell that wouldn't be suppressed by an AOE dispel during the AOE dispel's duration. In 2E, &quot;transitory&quot; means spells without Advanced Duration... of which the minimum &quot;transitory&quot; duration is 1 turn.<br /> <br /> Example with Thyrsus Mage 1 and Obrimos Mage 2:<br /> Mage 1 has Potency 20 W/S up from his buddy with lots of time on his hands and Prime Arcana 4. Mage 2's initiative comes up first and they cast an Advanced Scale area combined praxis spell of Celestial Fire and Supernal Dispellation with a reach for Aggravated damage at Mage 1; the spell has a potency of 7 and a minimum duration of 1 turn and Mage 1 gets an exceptional success with a roll of 3, opting to ignore Withstands.<br /> <br /> Mage 2 uses 4 Mana to power the 2 Reach and doesn't need to use Sensory Range because he can just chuck the spell with an attack roll of Gnosis + Firearms/Athletics. With Fast Spells, Mage 1 could only apply defense to a chucked spell if they could apply defense to bullets; even if they could, they can't apply defense to or dodge an area spell anyway. Just for giggles, because Mage 2 has Fate 1, they specify that it will only suppress spells that don't hurt Mage 2.<br /> <br /> Mage 1 can't dodge this and, of course, can't counterspell it without Prime magic. His withstand of the CF from Potency 20 W/S is ignored because it's an area spell. Even if it didn't, it would be ignored because of the exceptional success. Even if it didn't, the Supernal Dispellation beats any Withstand of W/S. Even if it didn't, the Potency of 7 means it would dispel W/S even if it had been cast with Advanced Potency. Even if W/S was somehow from an attainment and thus couldn't be dispelled, its withstand rating would be ignored by Celestial Fire because of the exceptional success.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Just because the CF/SD spell is area effect spell doesnt negate mage 1's W/S Spell, it only gets suppressed if bypassed by the CF/SP spells ignore withstand effect from the ES. Without a ES the CF/SD spell needs potency 21)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So Mage 1 is in a &quot;large house or building&quot; sized area in which all spells are subject to ignores-withstand Supernal Dispellation and everything is subject to 7 points of aggravated from Celestial Fire (including beings in Twilight). Arguably neither his Spirit Armor nor Life Armor apply against this damage. Thankfully, Mage 1 has Life 4 and Mend as a rote so they cast Mend with a reach to heal aggravated damage... unfortunately the area dispel is still in effect and nullifies Mend because it is within the area during the duration (1 turn). The Supernal Dispellation would nullify ANY non-archmage spell because of the ignoring of withstands from exceptional success and, even if the Storyteller houseruled against that, Mend's Withstand wouldn't beat SupDisp's Potency of 7 even with Advanced Potency.<br /> <br /> Mage 1's player says: &quot;But wait! Mend is a transitory spell! It takes effect instantly and can't be dispelled.&quot; The Storyteller says: &quot;That is literally not what Transitory means. If you look at the rulebook, transitory just means it doesn't have Advanced Duration. The only reference to 'immediate' effects are on page 113 in a section saying what happens when a heal or damage spell etc is cast with an extended duration. If the spell takes effect immediately, it still gets dispelled immediately. The book does not say what you say it does.&quot;<br /> <br /> Supernal Dispellation:<br /> &quot;Supernal truths can never truly be unmade, but with this spell<br /> the mage may cast them back across the Abyss, effectively erasing<br /> any spell she comes across. This spell is not potent enough to<br /> dispel archmages\u2019 spells.<br /> A successful casting suppresses the spell for the Duration of<br /> Supernal Dispellation.&quot;<br /> </div> </div> </div>I think you mean mage 2 gets a ES here and his CF/SD spell chooses to ignore withstand right? You seem to like praxis spells, but rotes are nearly always better esp since you can get the 3 ES thing from the inspired condition. IF mage 2 is prety certain of getting a ES (and most masters/sdepts with rotes can probably be) then he doesnt need to combine it with SD, his CF can choose to just ignore the withstand on its own.<br /> <br /> Plus in order for the combined spell without a ES to overcome the w/s spell of mage 1 it needs a potency of 21. A potency 7 CF/SD spell without a ES wont breach mage 1's W/S spell<br /> <br /> I know what a transitory spell is thanks, i was merely doing the &quot;working&quot; of what supernal dispellation does so that you better understood what was going on and giving the various options you might have though feasible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> If an area spell treats all possible subjects within its area as its subject which each withstands separately, then it suppresses every spell cast in the area during its duration. Period. The only way for Mage 1 to escape Mage 2's spell is to escape the &quot;large house or building&quot; sized area if their Speed allows.<br /> <br /> This is why I think area spells treating everything within AOE as subject, which is otherwise limited, is bats*** f****** insane. If it's RAW, that's cool. Still insanely OP. </div> </div> </div>Not quite sure where the 4 mana spend comes from but the mage would need gnosis 4.<br /> <br /> I think you are missing the point, We can all accept its stupidly easy for mages to kill alot of people very quickly.<br /> <br /> The problem then becomes what do other the other mages do about it? This is the internal &quot;balance&quot; that mage games have. If you just think everything in Mage as a FPS or RTS combat scenario then ofc mages are going to beat everybody else but there are other things than just number of targets you can kill or whatever at play in game, or there should be. IE consequences, retaliation. Would you not think 2ce about murdering X cabal with a super area spell when you know that the same could happen to you, its one reason why sane mages opt for other maybe non-lethal tactics and why the seer/pentacle &quot;war&quot; is more like a cold war than a raging magical battle through the streets.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 12-14-2017, 02:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T11:16:44-08:00","id":1167716,"title":"","content":"Since the original behavior of Dispelling spells is to suppress until duration ends, I would say that even if using the Lasting Reach option, it would still be a continuous effect, like a buff/debuff and not recurring like an attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T11:45:32-08:00","id":1167727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1166761-balancing-wards-signs-dispels-supernal-veil?p=1167716#post1167716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since the original behavior of Dispelling spells is to suppress until duration ends, I would say that even if using the Lasting Reach option, it would still be a continuous effect, like a buff/debuff and not recurring like an attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm still not seeing how this would apply as a sweeping application if Dispel Magic or Supernal Dispellation to all new spells introduced into the radius.<br /> <br /> It would be slightly more understandable if the primary factor was Duration, but even then - the purpose of the spell is to suppress ongoing magic. The Fate application about selective application implies sifting through readily available spells. It's like when you cast an AoE with Fate to avoid hitting your allies. I doubt the application of selectively choosing applies if your teammates rush into the AoE after you've cast it. It's meant to be applied in the moment, with the subjects present.<br /> <br /> <br /> By reading the spell description, the only thing we know for sure is that Dispel and Dispellation work on current spells. At this point some people are extrapolating the AoE application to mean all new spell phenomenon are also included in the initial batch of suppressed spells. This is stated nowhere. The spell does not state it suppresses future targets. It only ever refers to spells currently existing at the time of Supernal Dispellation's casting.<br /> <br /> Now, it doesn't explicitly state to treat it as a damage/healing interval spell, yet it does function a lot like them by claiming Potency as its primary factor. So we know Potency is relevant here because, as they devs said, &quot;whatever factor you think of when you think of a more powerful version&quot; (paraphrasing). This tells us that Potency is needed to overcome whatever the spell is trying to deal with. My guess? Any spells currently on the table. You need as much Potency to make it useful to even bother casting the spell in the first place.<br /> <br /> Duration secondary, or an after thought, because a stronger version of Supernal Dispellation is not considered to be a longer-lasting spell. A stronger version is considered to be one that has a higher Potency.<br /> <br /> If Supernal Dispellation's application was a uniform suppression of all current and future magic in the area, it would make more sense that a more powerful version of it would be a longer lasting one, or Duration as primary factor. Because you're concerned with shutting the whole party down for as long as you see fit, only using Potency to either decide how many spells you can suppress or what Withstand threshold all spells need to beat in order to occur.<br /> <br /> <br /> This would also lead me to believe that if your suppressed spell was something you cast on yourself, it wouldn't matter if you left the radius, because you were caught with Supernal Dispellation. Your spell would remain suppressed even if you left the area (either until the duration expires, the spell is destroyed, or some other effect takes place to shield you).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">N/A</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","name":"kryptonitekrusher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T11:51:13-08:00","id":1167731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1166761-balancing-wards-signs-dispels-supernal-veil?p=1167716#post1167716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since the original behavior of Dispelling spells is to suppress until duration ends, I would say that even if using the Lasting Reach option, it would still be a continuous effect, like a buff/debuff and not recurring like an attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. If a person with an active spell enters a area effect dispellation zone then that spell would check of it gets suppressed or not as per how area scale work. It wouldnt be active until the next gnosis interval of the dispell caster.<br /> <br /> The question is when does the dispellaroon spell act whwn somebosy casts a spell with a duration of 1 turn. Hence why i was xonsidering what i would do with a control fire zone. This led me to the conclusion that it gets dispelled before it takes effect enougj to do its thing. Its not really stated clearly in the book though amd another intrrpreatain could be that the spell is fast enough to avoid the dispell. Until a faq or sommat its a open debate.<br /> <br /> Even the pulsing every gnosis interval os up for debate, i can see how that could be valid also since a mend spell with a duration acts like that. <br /> <br /> Maybe spells that default to potency primary always pulse on gnosis intervals if advanced enough duration....its not clear tbh","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 12-14-2017, 03:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T12:29:33-08:00","id":1167743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1166761-balancing-wards-signs-dispels-supernal-veil?p=1167731#post1167731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep. If a person with an active spell enters a area effect dispellation zone then that spell would check of it gets suppressed or not as per how area scale work. It wouldnt be active until the next gnosis interval of the dispell caster.<br /> <br /> The question is when does the dispellaroon spell act whwn somebosy casts a spell with a duration of 1 turn. Hence why i was xonsidering what i would do with a control fire zone. This led me to the conclusion that it gets dispelled before it takes effect enougj to do its thing. Its not really stated clearly in the book though amd another intrrpreatain could be that the spell is fast enough to avoid the dispell. Until a faq or sommat its a open debate.<br /> <br /> Even the pulsing every gnosis interval os up for debate, i can see how that could be valid also since a mend spell with a duration acts like that.<br /> <br /> Maybe spells that default to potency primary always pulse on gnosis intervals if advanced enough duration....its not clear tbh</div> </div> </div> </div>If your spell is over by the time Supernal Dispellation is cast, then it wouldn't be able to address your spell. If your spell is ongoing, and exists within Supernal Dispellation at the time of its casting, then it would be suppressed for the duration of Supernal Dispellation. At which point, once Supernal Dispellation expires, your spell would resume unless they used +2 Reach to make the suppression lasting and destroy it entirely.<br /> <br /> It's still immensely powerful if you could potentially clear a whole slew of stuff like shields, wards, buffs, hexes, etc. with just one spell and a few reach. Even at the risk of Paradox you could wipe the table clean of a whole bunch of stuff you don't want to deal with.<br /> <br /> But you have to wait til your turn to cast Supernal Dispellation if you're in combat. If your opponent is casting spells, like damage spells, that take effect immediately and dissipate - then how could could you possibly catch their 3-second spell when you have to wait until the end of their 3-seconds in order to cast your own 3-second spell?<br /> <br /> It would logically mean you need to apply your dispel to whatever is lingering on the table. If you've turned your fire damage spell into a recurring gnosis interval spell, then you've left it on the table to be dispelled.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">N/A</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","name":"kryptonitekrusher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T15:46:44-08:00","id":1167784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kryptonitekrusher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1166761-balancing-wards-signs-dispels-supernal-veil?p=1167743#post1167743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If your spell is over by the time Supernal Dispellation is cast, then it wouldn't be able to address your spell. If your spell is ongoing, and exists within Supernal Dispellation at the time of its casting, then it would be suppressed for the duration of Supernal Dispellation. At which point, once Supernal Dispellation expires, your spell would resume unless they used +2 Reach to make the suppression lasting and destroy it entirely.<br /> <br /> It's still immensely powerful if you could potentially clear a whole slew of stuff like shields, wards, buffs, hexes, etc. with just one spell and a few reach. Even at the risk of Paradox you could wipe the table clean of a whole bunch of stuff you don't want to deal with.<br /> <br /> But you have to wait til your turn to cast Supernal Dispellation if you're in combat. If your opponent is casting spells, like damage spells, that take effect immediately and dissipate - then how could could you possibly catch their 3-second spell when you have to wait until the end of their 3-seconds in order to cast your own 3-second spell?<br /> <br /> It would logically mean you need to apply your dispel to whatever is lingering on the table. If you've turned your fire damage spell into a recurring gnosis interval spell, then you've left it on the table to be dispelled.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wait, im assuming some form on anti-spell dispellation spell is in effect already and discussing what happens when you try to cast when in that area already. You obv can and need to counterspell transitory spells cast instantly already but does whatever SD spell that isnt pulsed every interval take effect immediatly or is there any lag in its dispel effect..<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T12:36:49-08:00","id":1167991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1166761-balancing-wards-signs-dispels-supernal-veil?p=1167670#post1167670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Wouldn\u2019t work unless it forced the subject of the spell to use their Withstand as Withstand can be voluntarily waived and that\u2019s the default of approach of someone being targeted by a benign spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm confused... that's exactly what I'm suggesting. Wards &amp; Signs doesn't seem to allow control of what spells are Withstood, but the default is that all &quot;hostile&quot; magic is Withstood by W/S. So what if you had a CT spell or rote which did the opposite: replace hostile with benign? From my reading of RAW, you can't actually control Withstands of spells you cast EXCEPT when you're dispelling one under your spell control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11153-bonerstorm","name":"bonerstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T12:46:17-08:00","id":1167993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kryptonitekrusher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1166761-balancing-wards-signs-dispels-supernal-veil?p=1167709#post1167709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Supernal Dispellation's primary factor is Potency, like an attack spell. Attack spells pulse when you pump their Duration and reoccur at intervals relative to your Gnosis.<br /> *SNIP*</div> </div> </div> </div>That interpretation isn't supported by RAW. As discussed earlier, &quot;logically immediate effect&quot; spells are the ones which ping at intervals, NOT simply primary factor Potency spells. The base SD spell is unequivocally is NOT an immediate effect spell since it suppresses spells over their duration. The +2 Reach for Lasting Duration is a completely different story, though. THAT definitely is an immediate lasting effect, like an attack spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11153-bonerstorm","name":"bonerstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T13:06:12-08:00","id":1168002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1166761-balancing-wards-signs-dispels-supernal-veil?p=1167713#post1167713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just because the CF/SD spell is area effect spell doesnt negate mage 1's W/S Spell, it only gets suppressed if bypassed by the CF/SP spells ignore withstand effect from the ES. Without a ES the CF/SD spell needs potency 21)<br /> <br /> I think you mean mage 2 gets a ES here and his CF/SD spell chooses to ignore withstand right? You seem to like praxis spells, but rotes are nearly always better esp since you can get the 3 ES thing from the inspired condition. IF mage 2 is prety certain of getting a ES (and most masters/sdepts with rotes can probably be) then he doesnt need to combine it with SD, his CF can choose to just ignore the withstand on its own.<br /> <br /> Plus in order for the combined spell without a ES to overcome the w/s spell of mage 1 it needs a potency of 21. A potency 7 CF/SD spell without a ES wont breach mage 1's W/S spell<br /> <br /> *SNIP*<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>NOW we're cooking with gas!!! This is the conversation I wanted to have.<br /> <br /> According to a narrow (and unfortunately probably RAW) interpretation of Wards &amp; Signs, its Withstand ONLY applies to hostile magic directed at W/S's subject... NOT W/S itself or any other spells active on the subject. So a Disp or SuperDisp directed at a W/S would go against Arcana + ?Advanced Potency? Withstand instead of W/S's potency. So the only way to prevent W/S from being dispelled by a Potency of 8 in every case except for archmagi... is for W/S to have ANOTHER W/S with the first W/S as the second W/S subject.<br /> <br /> This means that absolutely no mage who isn't an arch can defend against the tactic I just described, regardless of whether there is an exceptional success. That means, storytelling-wise, it's really difficult to create high-level villains that can't be nuked by relatively low-level mages. Without the credible ability to defend, that leaves &quot;Oh yeah you can't find him and he has no personal connections to stuff&quot; or &quot;Oh yeah he has super powerful buddies who will nuke you if you nuke him.&quot;<br /> <br /> Shit... why does Kangaxx the Demilich ever leave the dungeon? Does that mean just operating on the margins and by proxy and indirect conflict? That's legit but I figured that'd be more Archmage play than just regular being-a-mage play.<br /> <br /> As an aside, because praxes exist, I definitely would houserule against Inspired triggering for spellcasting rolls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11153-bonerstorm","name":"bonerstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T13:17:19-08:00","id":1168009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1166761-balancing-wards-signs-dispels-supernal-veil?p=1167731#post1167731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep. If a person with an active spell enters a area effect dispellation zone then that spell would check of it gets suppressed or not as per how area scale work. It wouldnt be active until the next gnosis interval of the dispell caster.<br /> <br /> The question is when does the dispellaroon spell act whwn somebosy casts a spell with a duration of 1 turn. Hence why i was xonsidering what i would do with a control fire zone. This led me to the conclusion that it gets dispelled before it takes effect enougj to do its thing. Its not really stated clearly in the book though amd another intrrpreatain could be that the spell is fast enough to avoid the dispell. Until a faq or sommat its a open debate.<br /> <br /> Even the pulsing every gnosis interval os up for debate, i can see how that could be valid also since a mend spell with a duration acts like that.<br /> <br /> Maybe spells that default to potency primary always pulse on gnosis intervals if advanced enough duration....its not clear tbh</div> </div> </div> </div>It may be crazy and a hopeless cause, but I'm really trying to brainstorm ways to balance some of the more abusable aspects of Mage.<br /> <br /> Here's a thought: <br /> AOE spells are still subject to # of Subjects and Size of Subject limits on the same line in the effects tables. Conversely, multiple-subject spells may only target subjects that all fit within the space of the AOE described on the same line in the effects tables. Example from above would be that the SD could only suppress a maximum of 5 spells at one time. If more than 5, then go by distance from center and then randomness. If there are, say, 6 spells in the AOE, then 1 of them will randomly not apply.<br /> <br /> What do you think? Too limiting? Too hard to litigate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11153-bonerstorm","name":"bonerstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T13:34:08-08:00","id":1168012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bonerstorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1166761-balancing-wards-signs-dispels-supernal-veil?p=1167991#post1167991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm confused... that's exactly what I'm suggesting. Wards &amp; Signs doesn't seem to allow control of what spells are Withstood, but the default is that all &amp;quot;hostile&amp;quot; magic is Withstood by W/S. So what if you had a CT spell or rote which did the opposite: replace hostile with benign? From my reading of RAW, you can't actually control Withstands of spells you cast EXCEPT when you're dispelling one under your spell control.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m not sure I\u2019m following you. My point is that a person you cast a spell on can either Withstand, or not Withstand and that\u2019s a reflexive choice. Technically, you can already Withstand a beneficial spell, but since most people wouldn\u2019t do that there isn\u2019t a Withstand entry for beneficial spells. If you wanted to force someone to Withstand beneficial magic it wouldn\u2019t just be an inversion of Wards and Signs, it would have to be something that manipulated the character\u2019s ability to choose whether or not to Withstand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T15:06:19-08:00","id":1168030,"title":"","content":"If you're really that concerned about AoE effects, I'd say just don't allow spells that aren't specifically AoE in nature to be made AoE? That's the simplest change to get what you're going for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-16T02:59:01-08:00","id":1168144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1166761-balancing-wards-signs-dispels-supernal-veil?p=1168012#post1168012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019m not sure I\u2019m following you. My point is that a person you cast a spell on can either Withstand, or not Withstand and that\u2019s a reflexive choice. Technically, you can already Withstand a beneficial spell, but since most people wouldn\u2019t do that there isn\u2019t a Withstand entry for beneficial spells. If you wanted to force someone to Withstand beneficial magic it wouldn\u2019t just be an inversion of Wards and Signs, it would have to be something that manipulated the character\u2019s ability to choose whether or not to Withstand.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Originally posted by <b>bonerstorm</b> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1166761-balancing-wards-signs-dispels-supernal-veil?p=1167991#post1167991\">View Post</a></i><br /> <i>I'm confused... that's exactly what I'm suggesting. Wards &amp; Signs doesn't seem to allow control of what spells are Withstood, but the default is that all &amp;quot;hostile&amp;quot; magic is Withstood by W/S. So what if you had a CT spell or rote which did the opposite: replace hostile with benign? From my reading of RAW, you can't actually control Withstands of spells you cast EXCEPT when you're dispelling one under your spell control.</i> </div> </div> </div><br /> W/S provides the target with a withstand rating vs ALL magic that targets them directly friendly or hostile. In order for you to allow a spell to be cast on you without the W/S spell you'd need to cast Warding gesture on the person and except them. The W/S person cant choose not to apply W/S against magic cast on them even if they control the spell since if you control the W/S spell you can lower the potency as normal so any spell will effect you but you obv cant then raise it without recasting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 12-16-2017, 06:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-16T03:27:36-08:00","id":1168149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bonerstorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1166761-balancing-wards-signs-dispels-supernal-veil?p=1168002#post1168002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> NOW we're cooking with gas!!! This is the conversation I wanted to have.<br /> <br /> According to a narrow (and unfortunately probably RAW) interpretation of Wards &amp; Signs, its Withstand ONLY applies to hostile magic directed at W/S's subject... NOT W/S itself or any other spells active on the subject. So a Disp or SuperDisp directed at a W/S would go against Arcana + ?Advanced Potency? Withstand instead of W/S's potency. So the only way to prevent W/S from being dispelled by a Potency of 8 in every case except for archmagi... is for W/S to have ANOTHER W/S with the first W/S as the second W/S subject.<br /> <br /> This means that absolutely no mage who isn't an arch can defend against the tactic I just described, regardless of whether there is an exceptional success. That means, storytelling-wise, it's really difficult to create high-level villains that can't be nuked by relatively low-level mages. Without the credible ability to defend, that leaves &quot;Oh yeah you can't find him and he has no personal connections to stuff&quot; or &quot;Oh yeah he has super powerful buddies who will nuke you if you nuke him.&quot;<br /> <br /> Shit... why does Kangaxx the Demilich ever leave the dungeon? Does that mean just operating on the margins and by proxy and indirect conflict? That's legit but I figured that'd be more Archmage play than just regular being-a-mage play.<br /> <br /> As an aside, because praxes exist, I definitely would houserule against Inspired triggering for spellcasting rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Indeed. A mage with a W/S spell on him gains the extra withstand but the W/S spell itself doesnt. This is where you really need to use veiling spells on the W/S spell and just hope it doesnt get spotted to get dispelled <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> This isnt D&amp;D there is unlikely to be any solo NPC big bad mage that can take on a multiple people. Chronicles just isnt set up like that so if you throw solo things at groups then it will end badly for the solo person.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><i> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Originally posted by <b>kryptonitekrusher</b> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1166761-balancing-wards-signs-dispels-supernal-veil?p=1167709#post1167709\">View Post</a></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Supernal Dispellation's primary factor is Potency, like an attack spell. Attack spells pulse when you pump their Duration and reoccur at intervals relative to your Gnosis.<br /> *SNIP*</span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That interpretation isn't supported by RAW. As discussed earlier, &quot;logically immediate effect&quot; spells are the ones which ping at intervals, NOT simply primary factor Potency spells. The base SD spell is unequivocally is NOT an immediate effect spell since it suppresses spells over their duration. The +2 Reach for Lasting Duration is a completely different story, though. THAT definitely is an immediate lasting effect, like an attack spell. </div> </div> </div>As much as it wouldnt let me have a antimagic zone im begining to come round to the idea that Dis/SupDis is a logically immediate effect (its just useless without sticking some duration into the spell or you use the lasting reach.)<br /> <br /> If cast a 1 turn SupDis at a honing the form spell it's just suppressed for the turn i cast it on, if i use the lasting effect then the honing spell is destroyed and the SupDis ends also. An immediate effect.<br /> <br /> If there is a long duration SupDis spell area zone with the lasting reach effect that has a duration of say an hour and any spell that enters gets suppressed with a lasting duration/ destroyed.(so technically should still be in spell control just perm suppressed not destroyed but whatever). This is odd, a spell with X duration that has a Y duration effect, it doesnt seem right. (EDIT: i realise that the mending spell also sorta does this, its effects are lasting and it can have an area KEK)<br /> <br /> However if i cast a scene long duration SupDis over a area with the lasting reach that destroys all the spells in the area immediately and then pulses every gnosis interval and again immediately destroys all spells in the area when it pulses, this seems to make more sense? It makes the same sense as an area mend spell, its effects are also lasting.....<br /> <br /> If you dont use the lasting effect then any spells in the area are suppressed for the duration of the Sup/Dis spell and when it recasts on the gnosis interval any new spells in the area also get suppressed too.<br /> <br /> I think you just have to decide if Dis/SupDis spells count as an immediate effect or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 12-16-2017, 06:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-16T03:46:20-08:00","id":1168150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1166761-balancing-wards-signs-dispels-supernal-veil?p=1168144#post1168144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> W/S provides the target with a withstand rating vs ALL magic that targets them directly friendly or hostile. In order for you to allow a spell to be cast on you without the W/S spell you'd need to cast Warding gesture on the person and except them. The W/S person cant choose not to apply W/S against magic cast on them even if they control the spell since if you control the W/S spell you can lower the potency as normal so any spell will effect you but you obv cant then raise it without recasting.</div> </div> </div> </div>No it doesn\u2019t, it specifically says that it only works against hostile magic. In other words as a buff to Withstand it works exactly like regular Withstand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-16T05:02:11-08:00","id":1168157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1166761-balancing-wards-signs-dispels-supernal-veil?p=1168150#post1168150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No it doesn\u2019t, it specifically says that it only works against hostile magic. In other words as a buff to Withstand it works exactly like regular Withstand.</div> </div> </div> </div>How does it know if a spell is hostile or not exactly? the following text only says &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">When the subject is the target of a spell, that spell is Withstood with the Potency of Wards and Signs.</span></span>&quot; This suggests that its all spells that target the thing as it doesnt say target of a hostile spell here.<br /> <br /> Unless im missing something about how the spell can tell the difference between a hostile and non hostile spell or the text that says you can lower a spells withstand voluntarily except by lowering its potency perm i think its just a fluff error.<br /> <br /> Casting a invis spell on somebody to hide them from their cabal mates might be considered hostile magic but how would the W/S spell know? A mage might not want the bad guys making him invis to his cabal mates (yet still visible to the enemy) right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 12-16-2017, 08:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-16T06:06:11-08:00","id":1168166,"title":"","content":"I suppose if you ignore the flavor text, it is left vague, but the flavor text states the following as Mrmdubois has stated:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> By cloaking her subject in Aetheric symbols of victory and indomitability, the mage shields the subject from the effects of hostile magic. </div> </div> </div>It states Hostile Magic and in my mind when you are a target of Wards and Signs you can consciously control when it uses Withstand and when it does not. The intent of the spell is to protect the subject from spells that would cause them harm so interpret that as you will. As we all know, Core Rulebooks are guidelines and not written in stone how to do things and the ST has the final interpretation, but it seems the spirit of this spell is to protect the subject not make them a deflector shield for spells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-16T06:06:35-08:00","id":1168167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1166761-balancing-wards-signs-dispels-supernal-veil?p=1168157#post1168157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How does it know if a spell is hostile or not exactly? the following text only says &amp;quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">When the subject is the target of a spell, that spell is Withstood with the Potency of Wards and Signs.</span></span>&amp;quot; This suggests that its all spells that target the thing as it doesnt say target of a hostile spell here.<br /> <br /> Unless im missing something about how the spell can tell the difference between a hostile and non hostile spell or the text that says you can lower a spells withstand voluntarily except by lowering its potency perm i think its just a fluff error.<br /> <br /> Casting a invis spell on somebody to hide them from their cabal mates might be considered hostile magic but how would the W/S spell know? A mage might not want the bad guys making him invis to his cabal mates (yet still visible to the enemy) right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Presumably, by working with regular Withstand, by using the reflexive reaction to magic cast on them that characters are entitled to. In other words the spell doesn\u2019t decide, it relies on the decision to be made for it by the person under Wards and Signs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-16T07:13:30-08:00","id":1168182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1166761-balancing-wards-signs-dispels-supernal-veil?p=1168167#post1168167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Presumably, by working with regular Withstand, by using the reflexive reaction to magic cast on them that characters are entitled to. In other words the spell doesn\u2019t decide, it relies on the decision to be made for it by the person under Wards and Signs.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I read &quot;shields the target from hostile magic&quot; to mean magic cast at you by a hostile mage since what could count as a &quot;hostile&quot; spell could be up for debate.<br /> <br /> I can see an argument that the ability to not withstand a spell works on any withstand rating you have it just seems odd that the mage can control the spell in such a way esp if it was cast by another mage. Bobs W/S spell on Tim yet Tim gets to decide what Bobs spell works on seems odd. If i imagine choosing not to withstand something as exposing yourself even through spells that otherwise would protect you then i can just about accept it.<br /> <br /> I know Tim would really rather not be cut off and made invis from his cabal mates by having a supernal veil spell cast on him by his opponents (that are fated to ignore the veil) and would really like the W/S withstand to work on that nasty veiling spell since Tim considers it hostile. If Bob wanted to cast supernal veil on Tim and himself so they can escape instead and Tim considers this not to be hostile then he can choose not to withstand it.<br /> <br /> TL/DR If a mage withstands something its considered hostile. If he doesnt withstand it its not considered hostile. The act of wanting to withstand a spell means its hostile (Levitation is withstood only if the mage unwilling but still has a default stamina withstand anyway). Normally a mage cant withstand vs a supernal veil spell cast on him by a hostile mage since that spell doesnt have a withstand rating or allow one for being unwilling but having W/S on you allows you to decide its hostile and therefore get a withstand vs it or not, whichever you decide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-17T07:09:53-08:00","id":1168363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1166761-balancing-wards-signs-dispels-supernal-veil?p=1168157#post1168157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does it know if a spell is hostile or not exactly?</div> </div> </div> </div>....magic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-22T23:53:37-08:00","id":1169837,"title":"","content":"The way I read it is that, whether or not W/S is under your spell control, IT Withstands &quot;hostile magic&quot; and not you.<br /> <br /> Meaning:<br /> A) It works on any hostile effect that has you as a subject (hostile being defined by caster intent, common sense and GM fiat)<br /> B) Since the spell is withstanding and not you, you can't control whether it withstands a spell (though since it only works on &quot;hostile&quot; magic it really doesn't matter)<br /> <br /> Examples:<br /> A) Your sexy witch/warlock friend is playing wizarding BDSM with you and casts a bashing attack spell. Since the intent is not hostile (the intent is sexy times) the spell is NOT withstood by W/S.<br /> B) Your mortal enemy wants to embarrass you by turning your hair pink and, to his chagrin, you really don't mind because you wanted to get it dyed anyway. Regardless, no matter how much you want free pink hair, W/S withstands the spell because the intent is hostile.<br /> <br /> Regardless, HERE'S THE REAL QUESTION:<br /> When someone casts Supernal Veil on you does it work on all active spells that have you as their subject? Or is it useless in that scenario unless you use Scale to cover each spell separately? That's a BFD when it comes to making that spell useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11153-bonerstorm","name":"bonerstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T06:17:56-08:00","id":1169902,"title":"","content":"Each spell must be a factored in subject of the veil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T17:36:26-08:00","id":1170048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1166761-balancing-wards-signs-dispels-supernal-veil?p=1169902#post1169902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Each spell must be a factored in subject of the veil.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What I figured. Unfortunately, that's a really narrow benefit. Presumably Supernal Veil veils itself too for free? Otherwise that'd really spoil the point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11153-bonerstorm","name":"bonerstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T17:45:42-08:00","id":1170051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bonerstorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1166761-balancing-wards-signs-dispels-supernal-veil?p=1170048#post1170048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> What I figured. Unfortunately, that's a really narrow benefit. Presumably Supernal Veil veils itself too for free? Otherwise that'd really spoil the point.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well with one reach its 5 spells concealed which ain't such a small deal. I'd figure that's the intent of the spell, or else it kinda counters what it's supposed to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T19:28:55-08:00","id":1170067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bonerstorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1166761-balancing-wards-signs-dispels-supernal-veil?p=1170048#post1170048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I figured. Unfortunately, that's a really narrow benefit. Presumably Supernal Veil veils itself too for free? Otherwise that'd really spoil the point.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a Veiling spell it has to be actively looked for with Prime Mage Sight, or a spell designed to detect other spells. Which works fine in most situations, but in Mage there isn\u2019t a perfect setup that can\u2019t be countered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}